{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me","id":5001,"title":"Teenager scares the living **** out of me.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-07T05:58:14-08:00","id":5001,"title":"Teenager scares the living **** out of me.","content":"Allright... I'm going to try not being a misanthrope for a little bit.<br /> <br /> Here's the deal. I'm working on a campaign that is going to be run when the Dragon Blood book drops. Yeah, I know that's more than a year out, but I'm that kind of planner.<br /> <br /> The game is going to be set in oWoD, and it's a sub campaign of a oWoD/Exalted crossover. All of the PCs are going to be high-school students who Exalt as DB. What I'm interested in hearing about from you guys are all of the mean things that other kids did to you in high-school. I have my own short list, but I grew up during a certain era, and I got pretty good at avoiding being on the receiving end of things. Essentially, I'm looking for fuel to power my Exalt-high clique-drama.<br /> <br /> So... Share with me all of the ways in which teenagers have made your life miserable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/219-zid","user":"Zid","date":". 11-07-2013, 10:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/219-zid","name":"Zid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T07:09:04-08:00","id":5042,"title":"","content":"May I suggest reading Gantz (at least the first part)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T07:10:40-08:00","id":5044,"title":"","content":"You may, and I will!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/219-zid","name":"Zid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T07:54:20-08:00","id":5068,"title":"","content":"I feel like something interesting could be done with 15 &quot;squads&quot; of one of each Element each, with a single Lunar and Solar in each. Each squad would have a unique pairing of Solar and Lunar castes. And one Sidereal advisor of each Caste would advise 3 of those groups each.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T08:15:33-08:00","id":5083,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I wouldn't introduce any other exalt until later. I'd possibly look at shards not sure it has a modern exalt section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T09:04:12-08:00","id":5115,"title":"","content":"It's not a shards game. It explicitly takes place in the cWoD. Exalts have just made a come-back due to a shift in the cosmos. It's going to play out a lot like a cross between &quot;Heros&quot;, &quot;X-Files&quot;, and &quot;Lord of The Flies&quot;. I'm pretty sure the campaign is going to deal with the themes of teen suicide and gun violence. The only other exalt type that I know will make an appearance is going to be an Infernal, which will be given to the kid who's at the bottom of all the crap at the end of all this mess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/219-zid","name":"Zid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T09:44:14-08:00","id":5156,"title":"","content":"Remind me again what age interval high school is over there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T09:49:00-08:00","id":5161,"title":"","content":"Between the years of 14 and 18.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/219-zid","name":"Zid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T09:54:49-08:00","id":5169,"title":"","content":"The thing that hurt me the most was the constant social isolation. I was picked on, but that only happened because nobody cared. I was fair game because I was isolated. I had no one who would stand up for me, no one willing or able to have my back should things get abusive or violent.<br /> <br /> The reason I was isolated? Because I didn't like what the cool people liked. I prefered to read instead of play basketball, I liked to play Magic: The Gathering instead of whatever everyone else did at lunch (small talk? waste of time). My friends and I were treated like crap for no other reason than we were nerds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T09:58:49-08:00","id":5175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=5169#post5169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing that hurt me the most was the constant social isolation. I was picked on, but that only happened because nobody cared. I was fair game because I was isolated. I had no one who would stand up for me, no one willing or able to have my back should things get abusive or violent.<br /> <br /> The reason I was isolated? Because I didn't like what the cool people liked. I prefered to read instead of play basketball, I liked to play Magic: The Gathering instead of whatever everyone else did at lunch (small talk? waste of time). My friends and I were treated like crap for no other reason than we were nerds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't relate. People just ignored us and we were like two groups of 10-15 each. If anything we were bigger assholes to one another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T10:00:15-08:00","id":5177,"title":"","content":"Yea, I felt extremely isolated as well, which I think made me a target, particularly in Jr high. I had effectively skipped 2 grades in math, which further isolated me. I actually made friends with a lot of the high school kids then, because I was in a math class with them, but by the time I got to high school, all those guys graduated, which left me in a vulnerable spot.<br /> <br /> I remember having to fight a lot of fights because people just thought they could physically smack me around without consequence. My solution quickly became to escalate any slightly offensive contact into full-scale, you-better-fight-for-your-life-or-Imma-gonna-gouge-your-eyes-out violence, which seemed to work as a deterrent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/219-zid","name":"Zid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T10:07:31-08:00","id":5190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=5175#post5175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't relate. People just ignored us and we were like two groups of 10-15 each. If anything we were bigger assholes to one another.</div> </div> </div> </div>There were only about six or seven gamers in my whole school. Pretty much every other social group in the school had twice our number and was higher on the pecking order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T10:08:55-08:00","id":5191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=5190#post5190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There were only about six or seven gamers in my whole school. Pretty much every other social group in the school had twice our number and was higher on the pecking order.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose the issue has everything to do with the pecking order. More to the point, we really didn't have one. Everyone just grouped up sometimes talked to other people in other groups but didn't even bother. It was very chill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T10:11:35-08:00","id":5194,"title":"","content":"You don't notice the pecking order until it's hurting you. Most groups were roughly equal on the totem pole, so they just ignored each other. Cheerleaders and jocks got some preferential treatment sometimes. We caught crap even when we did things for other people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T10:13:49-08:00","id":5195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=5194#post5194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't notice the pecking order until it's hurting you. Most groups were roughly equal on the totem pole, so they just ignored each other. Cheerleaders and jocks got some preferential treatment sometimes. We caught crap even when we did things for other people.</div> </div> </div> </div>The school had like about two thousands students it's hard to have a &quot;popular&quot; group when there are so many and no one cares.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T10:29:07-08:00","id":5208,"title":"","content":"I never cease to be surprised that the blatantly ridiculous/overplayed horror of US high schools on TV shows<i> apparently is not overplayed at all. </i><br /> <br /> It's weird and scary, from a broader social view.<br /> <br /> EDIT: like, &quot;pecking order?&quot; What? How!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T10:30:28-08:00","id":5209,"title":"","content":"If I wanted to discuss teenagers being awful to each other, I'd pretty much just file it all under &quot;bullying.&quot; Men tend to bully by calling people names, forcing them to do embarrassing things and, of course, beating the shit out of them. Women tend to be a bit subtler, using emotional manipulation, social sabotage and ostracism to get their point across. A good rumor can do as much damage, or more so, than a good beating, and nothing hurts quite as bad as the feeling of being all alone.<br /> <br /> Thing is, you can see most of that when they're still kids. Adolescence introduces the fun of sexuality into the mix, not to mention drugs, alcohol and the emergence of psychological disorders (many of which only begin to appear around this time). Teenagers love to experiment, and love to pressure others into experimenting with them, which is why you tend to see a lot more drugs and alcohol at parties than anywhere else.<br /> <br /> With sex comes issues of homosexuality and gender-queerness, sexual humiliation (calling people sluts, spreading photos of them semi-clothed or nude, etc.), sexual intimidation (using social pressures to convince someone to have sex with you) and flat-out rape (of both the forcable and date-rape varieties). Thing is, a lot of teenagers don't even realize when they do these things that it's wrong- they haven't really evolved a proper moral compass yet, and so their ability to distinguish good and evil is mostly a matter of what feels good and what doesn't. Usually, they only realize they've done something wrong when the principal calls them into his office, or their parents yell at them, or- in extreme cases- when the police come knocking.<br /> <br /> Teenagers are in a weird place- they're adult enough to be given some adult responsibilities, but too childlike to be given the rights of an adult (when, of course, they'd like it to be the other way around). They struggle to deal with their hormones and emotions, try to develop their identities, and generally just transition from childhood to adulthood, and in the meantime, society starts placing tons of pressures on them. This cauldron of pressure and emotion naturally leads to problems, and what happens to them as adults tends to be a result of how they handle this transitional period. This doesn't excuse the shitty things they do, but it does put a lens on them- they're literally adult children, and ought to be considered as such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T10:37:45-08:00","id":5213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=5208#post5208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: like, &quot;pecking order?&quot; What? How!</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't an official, recognized thing like tv shows sometimes have. It was more like the rest of the world, where the downtrodden stay on the bottom and get ignored and the pretty, rich, or otherwise &quot;important&quot; people stay at the top.<br /> <br /> Still, the people most likely to directly harass me were the jocks on the football team. How stereotypical can you get?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T10:44:14-08:00","id":5220,"title":"","content":"Watch you the hell out of some Revolutionary Girl Utena.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T10:49:06-08:00","id":5230,"title":"","content":"Teenage girls are crazy, I can say that much. Middle school was the worst though - by highschool, usually the worst I got was that -look- when I tried to join a conversation. Whenever I tried to say something, everyone would just snap their heads around and give me this death glare in dead silence. It took awhile to learn how to talk in a group again, after a couple years of that.<br /> <br /> But in late middleschool, it really ran the gamut. I've had everything from the nicknames (&quot;Walrus, ort-ort-ort&quot; and &quot;Dracula&quot; namely, because after my braces were taken off my canines looked kinda fangy until the day they were ground down) to the passive-aggression (&quot;Really? You got me THIS for Christmas? Ugh.&quot;) to the good old &quot;grab her by the hair as you pass in the hall and slam her face into a locker door&quot; because why the hell not. (This last one was later followed up by the girl making a super-overwrought, sobbing apology in front of everyone to make herself look like such a wonderful person)<br /> <br /> The worst though was when I went to a friends' house with a group of girls (other friends) for a sleepover. The mood was rather silly and one girl got all OMG LET'S PLAY HIDE AND SEEK. Aren't we old for that?/okay, whatever. So we all go off and hide...<br /> <br /> Half an hour later, I'm wondering what the hell, so I wander back to the living room to find they've all been sitting there watching a movie without me.<br /> <br /> School was a fun time. I'm a grown-ass adult now, but I still flinch around teenagers because I half expect it to start all over again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":41,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/41-silverwinglie","user":"silverwinglie","date":". 11-07-2013, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/41-silverwinglie","name":"silverwinglie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar41_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T11:30:55-08:00","id":5261,"title":"","content":"Hmm, what\u2019s the general \u2018tone\u2019 you\u2019re going for? I can recommend a bunch of high-school centric entertainment, but it\u2019s mostly realistic/less dark than I think you want? Although maybe I\u2019m misreading into the \u201csuicide and gun violence\u201d stuff.<br /> <br /> Either way, the thing I\u2019ve always liked about good high school stories is the combination of that age range being primarily dominated by personalities that treat everything as the most important/devastating/enjoyful/whatever experience that has ever occurred anywhere, the inherent confusion hormones/lack of meaningful experience wreck, and a social environment that elevates/devastates participants seemingly on a whim.<br /> <br /> Letting \u2018big moments\u2019 (suicides, gun violence, grievous instances of bullying, etc.) be the major drama movers* is easier to grok/plan out, but also squashes a lot of the fun nuance. This isn\u2019t to say that those things are bad or shouldn\u2019t be represented, but they\u2019re usually events so large that the range of acceptable emotional reactions is almost predetermined. Whereas things like intra-clique friendship (especially if you choose something besides stereotype to divide cliques into) or romance (where declarations of love emerge within weeks, everyone\u2019s unsure of how to navigate sex, and your romantic activities raise or lower your reputation based on criteria picked to be as contradictory/minefieldy as possible) are dynamic and can be influenced greatly by the players, rather than just having them react.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*Note: Not saying this is what you\u2019re doing, this is just my thoughts from watching a lot of this stuff.</span><br /> <br /> Plus, all of that is just the drama of regular high school, i.e. one that presumes your teenagers DON\u2019T have super powers and have to deal with supernatural phenomenon. Which, now that I\u2019m thinking of it, means you should probably go and watch/re-watch the first three seasons of Buffy the Vampire Slayer so that you can just raid the episodes for ideas on how to represent high school anxiety through the prism of monsters and powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/870-side-item","name":"Side Item","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar870_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T12:03:44-08:00","id":5284,"title":"","content":"Can I ask what South Miami School? I came from Krop myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T12:08:11-08:00","id":5289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Side Item</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=5261#post5261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, what\u2019s the general \u2018tone\u2019 you\u2019re going for? I can recommend a bunch of high-school centric entertainment, but it\u2019s mostly realistic/less dark than I think you want? Although maybe I\u2019m misreading into the \u201csuicide and gun violence\u201d stuff.<br /> <br /> Either way, the thing I\u2019ve always liked about good high school stories is the combination of that age range being primarily dominated by personalities that treat everything as the most important/devastating/enjoyful/whatever experience that has ever occurred anywhere, the inherent confusion hormones/lack of meaningful experience wreck, and a social environment that elevates/devastates participants seemingly on a whim.<br /> <br /> Letting \u2018big moments\u2019 (suicides, gun violence, grievous instances of bullying, etc.) be the major drama movers* is easier to grok/plan out, but also squashes a lot of the fun nuance. This isn\u2019t to say that those things are bad or shouldn\u2019t be represented, but they\u2019re usually events so large that the range of acceptable emotional reactions is almost predetermined. Whereas things like intra-clique friendship (especially if you choose something besides stereotype to divide cliques into) or romance (where declarations of love emerge within weeks, everyone\u2019s unsure of how to navigate sex, and your romantic activities raise or lower your reputation based on criteria picked to be as contradictory/minefieldy as possible) are dynamic and can be influenced greatly by the players, rather than just having them react.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*Note: Not saying this is what you\u2019re doing, this is just my thoughts from watching a lot of this stuff.</span><br /> <br /> Plus, all of that is just the drama of regular high school, i.e. one that presumes your teenagers DON\u2019T have super powers and have to deal with supernatural phenomenon. Which, now that I\u2019m thinking of it, means you should probably go and watch/re-watch the first three seasons of Buffy the Vampire Slayer so that you can just raid the episodes for ideas on how to represent high school anxiety through the prism of monsters and powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Buffy was a big inspiration for this campaign. Basically, here's the deal. My players tend to play dick characters. In fact, they're kind of horrible people in general, but that's ok 'cause they're my friends. They've pretty much told me that they're itching to play dick high school kids and really engage in the high school clique deal. They plan on being the popular/mean kids.<br /> <br /> I don't plan on there being just shit tons of gun violence and suicides. In fact, there's only one instance of gun violence that is planned, and one suicide that comes as a result. Think of that crappy Carrie sequel, where the girl jumps off the building after being played particularly hard. It's going to come towards the end of the campaign, and it's supposed to be an 'Oh shit' type of moment, if it happens at all. As always, nothing in my stories is written in stone. It is an expected outcome based on how I expect my players will behave. I fully anticipate that their big bad is going to be an antagonist of their own making.<br /> <br /> Plus, all of this is going to be going on in the back drop of The Apocalypse.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/219-zid","name":"Zid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T12:09:53-08:00","id":5290,"title":"","content":"Like most people here, I was a total nerd. But I was a really BIG nerd and had an intensity in my eyes that years later I would learn most people interpreted as &quot;potential serial killer.&quot; I was asocial so this rarely became an issue for me, except for my RPG playing friends and the people from my church youth group. That last part would cause a lot of tension, however.<br /> <br /> How so? There was a girl I was very into. Importantly, I never pursued her; she was miles out of my league and I knew it. But I wanted to be closer to her, and she claimed she wanted the same from me. Yet she never interacted with me. At all. I would ignore this until it got to be too much for me, and then I'd ask to talk to her, she'd agree and show up with a female friend and I'd basically ask why she didn't want to talk to me.<br /> <br /> Her solution was, shall we say, less than intelligent. I doubt she asked or instructed her lover to do anything about this, but she clearly complained about me to him, and his solution was literally felonious. He threatened to kill me. On eight occasions. He was smart enough to do so without witnesses, but to say that he wasn't thinking everything through when he did this would be an understatement. He probably thought, &quot;I'm a karate black belt; I could take him.&quot; End of thinking.<br /> <br /> I didn't report him as a favor to the girl. But there is no chance in hell I'd ever forgive him for doing what he did, and knowing his intellect, he probably is proud of what he did back then. We only had two conversations where he did not threaten to kill me. In one, he merely threatened to shatter my hands. In the other, he explained he was a karate black belt, broke a board and explained that when he says he would shatter my hands, he literally means he would shatter my hands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have irregular access to the Web, so if you want to contact me, PM my account or email me at <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#3653445f5d5e57425f585358764f575e59591855595b\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"b3d6c1dad8dbd2c7daddd6ddf3cad2dbdcdc9dd0dcde\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/876-tsallak","name":"Tsallak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T12:11:19-08:00","id":5291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;grab her by the hair as you pass in the hall and slam her face into a locker door&quot; because why the hell not. </div> </div> </div>Man, the one time someone lay a hand on me in high school (a single punch), the police got involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T12:14:40-08:00","id":5299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hanged Man</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A little further north, actually. Santaluces High in Lantana. A big part of the problem wrangling a new school is that back then Donald &quot;Ambulatory Fungus&quot; Trump owned almost all of the suitable undeveloped land in Palm Beach County, and you can imagine precisely how many fucks that man gives about public education.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ugh. That sucks. Krop honestly wasn't any better. I had to practically relearn English grammar but Public Education feels like a joke in Florida. Like we were considered back when I went an &quot;A&quot; school but that just means we knew how to pass the FCat which was a joke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 11-07-2013, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T12:28:40-08:00","id":5311,"title":"","content":"I had a twin going into high school, and had a lot of fun.<br /> Only now do I look back and realize that all my friends were only friends with me because my brother was awesome. At least initially.<br /> By junior year (17), they were my friends in earnest. We played Magic the Gathering, talked about anime, got reasonably good grades to stellar grades. Most of us had glasses, but as the years progressed the glasses got replaced by contacts. Everyone's braces were off by the end of middle school, so the girls in my nerd-ish group were open to kissing but not much else. If we were called nerds, or dweeps, or whatever, it honestly didn't affect me much. Mostly because, to put it in Exalted terms, 'they were just extras to me'. Didn't know their names. Didn't care.<br /> <br /> What I got razed on the most was being on the co-ed swim-team. It was the nerdiest sports team in the whole school, and either the guys' bodies were perfect and pampered to the point of shaving their legs and being called 'gay', or the usual hairy teenager format (that'd be me). No other sports team at school considered us a valid 'sport'. But I got to get some exercise afterschool, earned a few medals, made some friends, and got to look at women (and yes, one or two men) in school swimsuits. People outside the swim team just didn't get it when they made fun of me. I was living the dream, even if I didn't get a girlfriend in time for prom or whatever.<br /> <br /> Middle School, however.....<br /> I hated middle school. I always will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":306,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","user":"Brasstreader","date":". 11-07-2013, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T12:28:54-08:00","id":5312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=5289#post5289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Buffy was a big inspiration for this campaign. Basically, here's the deal. My players tend to play dick characters. In fact, they're kind of horrible people in general, but that's ok 'cause they're my friends. They've pretty much told me that they're itching to play dick high school kids and really engage in the high school clique deal. They plan on being the popular/mean kids.<br /> <br /> I don't plan on there being just shit tons of gun violence and suicides. In fact, there's only one instance of gun violence that is planned, and one suicide that comes as a result. Think of that crappy Carrie sequel, where the girl jumps off the building after being played particularly hard. It's going to come towards the end of the campaign, and it's supposed to be an 'Oh shit' type of moment, if it happens at all. As always, nothing in my stories is written in stone. It is an expected outcome based on how I expect my players will behave. I fully anticipate that their big bad is going to be an antagonist of their own making.<br /> <br /> Plus, all of this is going to be going on in the back drop of The Apocalypse.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that does sound interesting. And again, wasn't thinking of you when I mentioned overuse of those big events, just what I've seen (Degrassi...uhh, *cough*).<br /> <br /> But, if the default player is less the person being mocked and more the ones doing the mocking, there's a whole bunch of stuff that shows how internecine conflict within a dominant group can run rampant. Mean Girls and Heathers for example are pretty explicitly about this (and are actually fun to watch). You could* also check out Friday Night Lights (the show) for where being the golden gods in school still means you have to handle all the normal teenage bullshit, plus heightened expectations that threaten to crush you if you make the slightest misstep (which is usually outside your control).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Read as: Should. It's a great show everyone.</span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tsallak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=5290#post5290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In one, he merely threatened to shatter my hands. In the other, he explained he was a karate black belt, broke a board and explained that when he says he would shatter my hands, he literally means he would shatter my hands.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to start off by saying that that whole situation sounds rightly fucked and you shouldn't have had to go through it.<br /> <br /> That being said, the quoted part makes it sound like this guy carried around wooden boards everywhere with him so he could demonstrate his sick black belt skillz, a mental image which highly amuses me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/870-side-item","name":"Side Item","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar870_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T13:18:19-08:00","id":5357,"title":"","content":"By the 14-18 year range, the worst of it had passed for me. I had a good class, and I went to a school where &quot;popular&quot; and &quot;doing well&quot; were not exclusive properties; in fact, they often went hand in hand. Add to this that the science program (not really the right word for it, but a focus on math, physics and other natural sciences) I went to had a way of attracting slightly nerdy folks. We could sit and program our TI calculators during break. I was actually pretty good at it for a while there.<br /> <br /> The worst for me was in middle school, around 9-12. I was kind of slow, overweight, timid and just not used to talking to people, making me too easy to push around to not do it. I never got into any physical fights, but many were the breaks when I sat in a corner of the schoolyard just imagining things. Some people did see my weakness and pounced on it, but I honestly don't remember much in particular of what happened. Certainly not the kind of physical stuff you can see in American high school drama. More like snide remarks and making jokes at my expense. It wasn't fun, but I lived.<br /> <br /> Funnily enough, one of my biggest bullies became my best friend in high school. I later went to his wedding. Funny how things turn out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T13:29:06-08:00","id":5369,"title":"","content":"Yea, I think the 14-18 range, the worst had passed for me too. Most of my bad times were in jr. high, which is 13-14 (7th and 8th grade). By the time I finally got in highschool, I'd managed to make some friends and fit in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/219-zid","name":"Zid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T13:54:50-08:00","id":5388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=5291#post5291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Man, the one time someone lay a hand on me in high school (a single punch), the police got involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>The one time in high school the cops got involed with something that happened to me, I was the one charged with assault, mostly because I was a guy who was assaulted by girls. BTW, anger management classes are boring and pointless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T14:15:32-08:00","id":5407,"title":"","content":"I went to a male-only highschool... man was it horrible, it was very similar to a cantina or a reformatory. I never got along with most of my classmates, I preferred to keep a low profile and make drawings while all the other guys were playing sports or talking about their macho adventures.<br /> <br /> The first year there were these two a-holes who tried to pick on me and made jokes about my clothes. They stopped the day they tried to hit me with the class door while I walked distracted through the hallway. I don't know how I did it, but it was as if I had a spider sense in that second, I stopped the door with the palm of my hand and slammed it on their faces instead, perfect timing. It must have looked very cool, because I later noticed everyone else staring at me like &quot;well done man!&quot;. Those imbeciles never bothered me again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T14:46:05-08:00","id":5430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=5291#post5291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Man, the one time someone lay a hand on me in high school (a single punch), the police got involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was a very small private, religious school. No police, you just got taken up to the chapel to &quot;pray about it&quot;. It was a wonderful place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/41-silverwinglie","name":"silverwinglie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar41_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T14:52:52-08:00","id":5439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>silverwinglie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=5430#post5430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This was a very small private, religious school. No police, you just got taken up to the chapel to &quot;pray about it&quot;. It was a wonderful place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope that was sarcasm, because anywhere you can get away with physically abusing another person is not a wonderful place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T14:59:44-08:00","id":5446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=5439#post5439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hope that was sarcasm, because anywhere you can get away with physically abusing another person is not a wonderful place.</div> </div> </div> </div>It absolutely was sarcasm. The staff also routinely harassed me - there was one occasion where, for a gym class grade, we were required to attend a particular protest. I refused, and after going back and forth with the administration, it was decided that to make up for my absence I'd be packing lunches for all the students who were going. Whatever.<br /> <br /> But as a result of that, I was later on accused of attempting to &quot;corrupt&quot; the other students by &quot;making a show of&quot; refusing to go (I did no such thing), and ended up in the chapel to &quot;pray it out&quot; for quite some time. This place was fairly sick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/41-silverwinglie","name":"silverwinglie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar41_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T15:27:34-08:00","id":5476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>silverwinglie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=5446#post5446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It absolutely was sarcasm. The staff also routinely harassed me - there was one occasion where, for a gym class grade, we were required to attend a particular protest. I refused, and after going back and forth with the administration, it was decided that to make up for my absence I'd be packing lunches for all the students who were going. Whatever.<br /> <br /> But as a result of that, I was later on accused of attempting to &quot;corrupt&quot; the other students by &quot;making a show of&quot; refusing to go (I did no such thing), and ended up in the chapel to &quot;pray it out&quot; for quite some time. This place was fairly sick.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm understanding what sort of protest that would have been, I think you made the right call. Congratulations on surviving with some semblance of sanity.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T15:34:23-08:00","id":5483,"title":"","content":"My time in secondary school was fairly good, and I was unusually immersed in the socialisation of it, at least until maybe the last year where I became so bored and contemptuous of everybody despite how generally pleasant they were towards me that I deliberately isolated myself, and became increasingly open with attitudes that were probably kind of disturbing to everybody considering what happened in the last few months.<br /> <br /> Or I at least tried to isolate myself, considering that nobody ever stopped talking to me and it was too late for anybody to not know my name.<br /> <br /> I also have an attitude that the place kind of disintegrated in the years after I no longer attended it, but trying to look back with a sense of objectivity makes me think that it's possible that it was actually kind of in shambles for the duration, and I just didn't really notice because I was so tremendously solipsistic.<br /> <br /> Heck, in my fifth year, there was a trip abroad in which not a single person who was part of my usual circles went, and pretty much everybody there were people who, in a conventional narrative, would have been merciless to me; it was a wonderful time.<br /> <br /> And the staff, despite how there were some who I think may have had questionable professional and ethical standards, all adored and respected me, even though I was a shoddy student (in terms of actually turning in work consistently) and, towards the end, was pretty open about questioning them to the point of contempt.<br /> <br /> It was... weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T12:54:00-08:00","id":6260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>silverwinglie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=5430#post5430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was a very small private, religious school. No police, you just got taken up to the chapel to &quot;pray about it&quot;. It was a wonderful place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I attended a private Episcopal elementary school for a few years.<br /> <br /> One day, I threatened to shove my middle finger up a girl's nose because she was being annoying and I was like seven years old. The adults went absolutely nuts because they thought I was flipping her the bird.<br /> <br /> I'd never seen or heard of &quot;the bird&quot; before, so I had no idea what their problem was. I was I just mimicking Jonny Five, the robot from <i>Short Circuit</i>, who had a third arm with all sorts of waldos, gizmos and manipulators. For years, I'd have fun by flipping out my hand, extending a random finger, and poking a keyhole that I wanted to &quot;unlock&quot; and stuff like that.<br /> <br /> For some reason, the adults absolutely refused to believe this was possible. Clearly, a child my age HAD to know what &quot;the bird&quot; was and HAD to be using it for precisely what they thought I was, because, Fuck You, Kid, you're a child and we know you're lying because We're The Adults.<br /> <br /> Seriously, if they had simply explained to me that it was a rude gesture and that I should never do it again, I'd honestly have never done it again and that would have been the end of it. The adults were less mature on this issue than the damned seven-year-old.<br /> <br /> Ruined a perfectly good field trip.<br /> <br /> <br /> As a Christian, I won't say that all &quot;religious&quot; schools are bad, but I can definitely see how they attract the &quot;holier than thou&quot; Pharisees for staff members. Hell, that was the problem with the Baptist Children's Home my parents worked at. The people in charge were more interested in keeping up appearances and housing as many warm bodies as possible rather than treating kids with VERY REAL psychological issues.<br /> <br /> It's not like the days of the early Church, where holding a position of authority meant risking your life. The threat of being targeted for death must have worked WONDERS for discouraging anyone seeking office for less than Godly intentions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T23:23:50-08:00","id":6656,"title":"","content":"I had more trouble in middle school than high school too. It was crowded and run by a city that tended to concentrate the elementary and middle school students that they considered troublemakers into a few schools to keep the rest of the schools tidy to showcase how good they were to anyone looking at the school system. They could not pull that shuffle around trick with the high schools since there were so few of them but since the smallest one in the city had over 2000 students the &quot;troublemakers&quot; kind of got lost in the crowds anyway.<br /> <br /> Besides the usual shoves and trips, book flips, hair pulls and the occasional locking of someone in a locker (in the junior high I went to the lockers in the old section of the school were the backless bolt to the wall type and one girl who was shoved into and locked in one was small enough to pull her legs up, plant them against the wall and push hard enough to rip the whole line of lockers off the wall) there were other nasty things some students would do to each other.<br /> <br /> I often got chased around by a gang of morons who never seemed to catch on to my simple trick of running to string them out and then suddenly turning on the one in the lead and using his own momentum to knock him flat and then taking off again to repeat it on the next. After a long while they finally stopped doing that, especially when they found out that if they did manage to catch me I would kind of snap and go rabid weasel on them (I had some issues back then\u2026.) and I think it actually scared them. Sometimes I spent more time in the office on detention than in class though I never started anything. <br /> <br /> There was a trick that I was never caught by because I would watch for it though others would walk into it from inattention. It was also kind of rare because it was dependent on the halls being full of standing people which usually only happened in the mornings when waiting for the section doors to be opened. It was called the \u201cpinball slot\u201d locally though it probably has other names and is easy to spot if you know the bullies by sight (and I knew every one of them in the school). The name came from them lining up in two queues with a space between them and when a victim walked into the empty space one of them would shove the person sidewise and the one across would shove back like a pinball between two lines of those kicker things on a pinball table. If the line was very long the victim would be quite disoriented and possibly injured by the time they were ejected out the other end of the column. <br /> <br /> Bombs in the bathrooms were another middle school favorite, they would either set them out of sight to give people ringing ears and headaches when they went off or else they would make compact waterproof ones and flush them to (or at least try to) make all the toilets geyser.<br /> <br /> By high school most of that nonsense was gone and the stuff that was left was more either malicious pranks or social attacks to humiliate rather than physically damage the target. Sure, there were still a few dim mooks that tried to intimidate people but they were relatively rare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T02:09:18-08:00","id":6692,"title":"","content":"High school for me is dimly recalled nowadays, blocked out somewhat by a good college career and social life I had afterwards. What I can recall is pretty much a blur of repressed emotions and an all-consuming rage and frustration that would burn down the whole state I reside in. There were the *worst* type of passive-aggressive bullies, teachers that should have retired a decade ago, insistent folk who thought they were helping but were really harming despite my protestations...the whole thing was pretty much something that engendered in me a desire to grow up to be Akira and psychic-nuke every last thing that came from that school system.<br /> <br /> That should probably give you by itself an idea of what my high school life was like. Details would...probably be uncomfortable for everyone, even if I could remember them well. It's something I've moved on from and would like to continue in that regard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/748-ultrafennec","name":"UltraFennec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar748_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T05:23:46-08:00","id":6747,"title":"","content":"I went to an art school. That didn't mean all that much- people went to their chosen classes (like actual drawing, acting, music, computer art, etc) and the other classes the school threw at us as an addition to make our grades seem impressive (the grading system in Israel is kinda weird). What ended up happening was that, because the school had mostly people who got bruised by school hierarchies BEFORE high school, that actual school had none. There were just lots of tiny groups of people who minded their own business, without mingling much. Which was kinda odd at times, but it ended up all right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/792-karpattata","name":"Karpattata","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T05:52:35-08:00","id":6764,"title":"","content":"Wow. It must have sucked hard for you guys.<br /> <br /> I went to a UK private school (\u00a36k a year). We had class sizes of 8-18, and 2-4 classes per age group.<br /> <br /> When the social clique for the 'cool kids' was about 8 people they didn't have the social capital to do more than throw abuse at each other. In classes that small the teachers hear everything, see everything and are empowered to act on anything.<br /> <br /> Sports teams were amusing too. I was CRAP at rugby but my Dad was a big fan and I wanted to make him happy so I just asked to get on the team. I was playing in the next match 2 weeks later against some other school. Sports weren't the way to be 'cool' at school. A Rugby team needs 15 players and some subs...we got lucky to have 15 players at all. If you wanted to play you were in. By the end of it I was a not bad Center too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> A-levels were the most amusing. That's 16-18 years for those who don't know. The school basically started an A-Level department in my year so we had...I think 5 people. You chose 4 subjects and spent your full school day just studying those. Maths had 4 students including myself, Chemistry 2, Physics 3 and Biology 3. And yes. Maths, Physics, Chemistry, Biology. I was a nerd/geek/whatever. The cunning of you will notice though that if class sizes for these subjects were running at 2-3 and we only had 5 students....there was a lot of science being covered by the A-Level group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T07:06:00-08:00","id":6794,"title":"","content":"Actually and I only learned this years after the fact I was viewed as something of a maverick that was marking time in High School and utterly bored by the whole experience..I was bullied in Junior High which when I was in school was 7th-9th grade which was 1981-1984. I had a lot of friends but very few went to my Junior High School. I had to choose a language and I chose French mainly because at the time I had a good friend in the class. The French teacher was a very unpleasant woman who went out of her way to be nasty to me. At one point she told my Dad that I didn't belong in her class as I was the son of a janitor and would never be able to afford a trip to France. The children I attended school with were the sons of Doctors, Lawyers, Jewelry store owners and such. I put up with and ignored the comments on how I dressed I honestly could have and still could care less I put up with the veiled threats, the pushing shoving and what not however when my best friend and his new best friend the friend from French class decided they had to be popular and I was such a target they turned on me I ignored it for a long time until one day I snapped. That day I had enough and told both of them I wouldn't put up with their insults we were supposed to be friends. This was my Mom's advice. It didn't work. I live in a rough neighborhood, but my family has lived in it since my great great Grandparents emigrated to America. I learned to fight my Mom insisted so did both of my sisters when my then friends touched me I fought back. Between that fight such as it was and my accidently shattering a kid's kneecap in gym class I was pretty much left alone to read my books which where either Science Fiction or Fantasy or Horror. In High School I was reunited with my friends from all over the city. I never cared about being popular, I still don't. I speak my mind and have since then I called bullies out in High School and since I tutored most of the football team no one messed with me. The only person that tried to bully me got the crap beat out of them by my Grandmother's next door neighbor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":293,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","user":"lncbill","date":". 11-09-2013, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T22:45:53-08:00","id":59531,"title":"","content":"Was anyone else kinda offended by the ageist tone of the first post? I mean, hell, being a teenager is hard enough without a bunch of random-ass adults holding a grudge against you. Anyway, I just started reading <a href=\"http://parahumans.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Worm</a>, and at least the <a href=\"http://parahumans.wordpress.com/category/stories-arcs-1-10/arc-1-gestation/1-01/\" target=\"_blank\">first chapter</a> contains a pretty graphic depiction of high school bullying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mort is sad because he died waiting for this post to show up. Poor, sweet Mort.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2121-a-sad-ghost","name":"A Sad Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T23:24:24-08:00","id":59561,"title":"","content":"Huh. Now I'm wondering if my rather pleasant school experience was atypical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T23:42:03-08:00","id":59567,"title":"","content":"How do people outside of the United States view bullying in schools? Is it a thing that happens often? Maybe you got lucky because you're Ottawasian. (I peeked at your profile to learn that because I am an ace internet sleuth)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mort is sad because he died waiting for this post to show up. Poor, sweet Mort.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2121-a-sad-ghost","name":"A Sad Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T23:56:04-08:00","id":59574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me#post5001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What I'm interested in hearing about from you guys are all of the mean things that other kids did to you in high-school.</div> </div> </div> </div>After school, when I walked by the other buses to get to my own, people would spit on me. Sometimes when I came back to homeroom, I'd find rotting cheese or dog poop in my desk. While running in gym, people would slam me against the wall. When we did push-ups, sometimes boys would make mooing noises. When eating lunch, I had food and those fruit juice pouches tossed at me.<br /> <br /> There was also regular stuff like having my locker broken into, getting beaten up, and having my stuff destroyed/stolen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=5291#post5291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Man, the one time someone lay a hand on me in high school (a single punch), the police got involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>I once sent another student to the emergency room because I bit a chunk of his arm off in self-defense, but that was atypical. I dislike violence and have always tried to avoid it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 01-28-2014, 03:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T00:04:41-08:00","id":59577,"title":"","content":"://////////","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mort is sad because he died waiting for this post to show up. Poor, sweet Mort.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2121-a-sad-ghost","name":"A Sad Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T01:15:34-08:00","id":59609,"title":"","content":"I was socially isolated and thus, as many here have also reported, picked on, since nobody cared. I was isolated because of various reasons.<br /> It started with me having grown up in a very different country, though I went to a german ambassadorial school it left me unaware of a lot of the social norms. It certainly didn't help at all, that I tried to change that by learning about the country's history. I pretty naively expected knowledge to help, but it merely set me apart even more. I got teased and hit for knowing things they didn't. I was even more of an outsider for having to say I belonged to another religion than was the norm, which I didn't even believe in, which just made it way, way worse. Since I wasn't attending their religious meetings and classes, I was lesser than them.<br /> Young adults will seemingly always believe the majority belief in class to be correct and as with everything else, punish deviance from the norm.<br /> <br /> During my entire school-life I spent every possible minute in the school library, though after a while I had to bring my own books since I had read everything but the most dry of literature after two years. But it was my only safe place, since I really desperately wanted to avoid home.<br /> <br /> I didn't really resist being hit or kicked, unless it went over a certain point. The instances in which I was actually kicked or hit with force were very few in comparison to the regular, stupid but playful ones.<br /> One of those instances was a girl that was into me but couldn't say it because of how it would make her look. About three years later she tried to explain to me, in tears. That was weird for someone who'd never been that close to anyone nor could quite grasp why someone would pretend to have been interested in me. Let alone fathom that she was actually sincere. I'm glad to say I decided I'd rather risk being made fun of for being so naive than risk actually hurting someone else emotionally, so I (awkwardly) managed to tell her that I didn't hold her behavior against her. At that point in time she was the only person in my life who smiled when she saw me. I didn't get it at the time, but I wasn't about to question the only bright spot in my life.<br /> <br /> That all only stopped when a group that kept hassling me for years got a chair thrown at them and suddenly were scared shitless of me. I wasn't even close to hitting one of them, but I was never bothered with hits and kicks again. Nor with a friendly smile.<br /> <br /> But I did become the psycho who obviously must be taking lots of drugs guy, which led to merry visits from teachers, police and concerned parents telling me how awful anyone who takes drugs is and thus I am. My classmates weren't bothered enough to not hassle me, but enough to not &quot;playfully&quot; assault me anymore or include me in games, which I had been allowed to participate in, even though I never got played fair, I still preferred it to total isolation.<br /> It didn't help that a supposed friend, who was the only one who listened to me at all, let me explain the rather complex strategy game I worked out with about 300 pieces of paper during class before joyfully mixing them up and throwing a handful out the window. I had one of my three rage-kinda-blackouts, where things got blurry but I still did remember what happened through a haze. I threw tables aside to get at him and the five boys present as well as one of the stronger girls had to grab onto me, and I still proceeded at a turtle's inevitable but slow pace towards the guy I wanted to really hurt.<br /> As you can imagine, it just added to my psycho reputation.<br /> <br /> When that idea finally died off, I was just the weird kid and my classmates went over to stealing my shoes and playing keep-away every break. The saddest part about this is that since this was the first time I was included in any kind of game again, I preferred it to not being interacted with, while hating being treated that way at the same time. Which of course, in addition to everything else, made it easy to justify for them, because they could argue (kinda rightly) that I wanted them to play this game with them and that it was totally harmless.<br /> That's something I'd highly recommend to use. People often end up in abusive relationships because it seems better than total isolation. It's hard to understand why the kid you may be trying to save from being bullied might get mad at you. But if you understand that they can't imagine themselves in a better relationship with people and don't want to lose that last bit of interaction they have outside of their home (which may suck even more) it can be a deliciously warped human thought process everyone gets.<br /> <br /> And that's when I failed class thanks to a teacher who hated me and didn't like being told the books and internet (whatever crazy thing that is) said something different than her, let alone questioning the validity of democracy as the holy grail of humanity.<br /> <br /> That was when I got into a class of nicer people, who gave me a chance. Being so used to being the outcast, I somewhat blew it by being a standoffish ass to a couple of them but was lucky enough to meet four other weird people, who liked fantasy, M:TG and sci-fi. And even rpgs. So I assembled my first gaming group and life kept getting better for quite a while.<br /> <br /> Everything after that really isn't worth telling, though it was beautiful to live through.<br /> I was being treated normally, with the normal amount of hassling but also with nice things and awkward interactions with girls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2UIUH9oaJnHMWIxcVdGMjNUYlE\" target=\"_blank\">3EX Martial Arts basic overview (Weapons, Armor, Attributes &amp; Abilities)</a>","edited":{"userid":366,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/366-edward-eldritch","user":"Edward Eldritch","date":". 01-28-2014, 04:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/366-edward-eldritch","name":"Edward Eldritch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T21:31:26-08:00","id":60435,"title":"","content":"Middle School was a little miserable, High School was smooth sailing.<br /> <br /> I fucking hated Elementary though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T21:44:16-08:00","id":60445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=5220#post5220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Watch you the hell out of some Revolutionary Girl Utena.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would agree if the PCs were Sidereals/Raksha, going to school with Gods and Fae. The surreal weirdness would fit pretty well...<br /> <br /> If it's a straight up teen action/drama, however, there are lots of high school anime with martial arts and elemental powers, but my fave is probably <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yuz01t_9wtg\" target=\"_blank\">Tenjou Tenge</a>. It's sister show, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nEJjI8AITas\" target=\"_blank\">Ikkitousen</a> has even more over-the-top action (and fanservice!), but might be more appropriate to a Celestial Exalted story as it's about modern teens being driven by the spirits of ancient warriors to reenact past battles by gathering armies of gangs and taking over each others' high schools...<br /> <br /> Either way, there's epic dickery in both shows! Enjoy!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T23:53:57-08:00","id":60526,"title":"","content":"I got beat up and paddled in Elementary.<br /> <br /> I got assaulted and into a fight in Middle School. Also kicked in the balls but that wasn't emotionally traumatizing. People tell me I won that fight for some reason.<br /> <br /> I witnessed fights in High School, a couple guys were assholes to me and somebody threw a rock at me. Or dirt clod.<br /> <br /> My second High School was awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T01:49:03-08:00","id":60567,"title":"","content":"I'm going to be blunt.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Fuck</b></i> public schools in America.<br /> <br /> Everything you see reported on in the news here? That's just the aftershow. High school in America is a fucking <i>microcosm</i> of what you see the news rant and rave about. All that abuse, mudslinging, horrendous behavior and miserable examples of human beings? Where the fuck do you think they learned that shit?<br /> <br /> Yes, I am VERY bitter and cynical about American culture in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/2480852/chapters/5503997\" target=\"_blank\">Glorious Echeladder Ascension Technique</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/287292-glorious-echeladder-ascension-technique-a-homestuck-exalted-crossover\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Topic</a><br /> <br /> &quot;Look, sometimes you just are in the mood to play the divinely empowered champion of the God of Farts. Mechanically optimized play is not the only way to enjoy playing your character.&quot; -Wise Old Guru","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1048-ryumaru","name":"Ryumaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1048_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T02:22:35-08:00","id":60589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=59561#post59561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. Now I'm wondering if my rather pleasant school experience was atypical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not. My experience was fairly pleasant and involved playing sports, having dozens of friends of both genders, and sharing a broad range of interests with my peers, including &quot;geeky&quot; ones. The only people didn't have fun in high school appeared to be the ones who were trying not to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T04:39:43-08:00","id":60632,"title":"","content":"Mine was rather pleasant as well. The first half involved me being a rather asocial shut-in who concentrated on grades and sometimes played RPGs with a few close friends. The second half I opened up, made a bunch of friends (boys and girls) and had a lot of fun. No school sports, but I did a lot of art, theatre and photography as extracurriculars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T04:50:43-08:00","id":60634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Sad Ghost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=59567#post59567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do people outside of the United States view bullying in schools? Is it a thing that happens often? Maybe you got lucky because you're Ottawasian. (I peeked at your profile to learn that because I am an ace internet sleuth)</div> </div> </div> </div>Largely non-existent in my neck of the woods. And I also kinda assume that every movie ever made grossly exaggerates the issue of American high schools, if only because the thought that every American teenager is psychotic, is kinda creepy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/635-slaunyeh","name":"Slaunyeh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T06:36:27-08:00","id":60700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slaunyeh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=60634#post60634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Largely non-existent in my neck of the woods. And I also kinda assume that every movie ever made grossly exaggerates the issue of American high schools, if only because the thought that every American teenager is psychotic, is kinda creepy.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because the high school experience par cinema is viewed through the lens of people who had bad high school experiences in all likelihood because they were told by the media they consumed they should have bad high school experiences. Life imitating art, in their case, which results in art imitating (their) life.<br /> <br /> Bullying is a thing, but it's never at the Biff Tannen levels in real life. In general, my high school frowned on bullying, and I'm not talking about the staff (who were generally not aware of these things because teenagers are very good at concealing things); students didn't tolerate endemic bullying of people. Even if they probably deserved it. But especially not because someone was doing well in a class. With an academic body 90% aimed at 4-year colleges (and the other 10% headed for the military) only a few kids were there to fuck around, and if they wanted to be problematic they were quickly socially isolated. Disrupting class generally got you the evil eye from everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T06:50:20-08:00","id":60714,"title":"","content":"I find the median high-school experience in America is directly correlated to what the &quot;feel&quot; of the school is. In my high-school experience, teachers were sympathetic but distant, which was symbolic of how the adults in the region I lived in treated their kid's in the time of my youth (generally speaking). The main concern when trouble popped up, for the teachers, was quietly and quickly resolving the situation and putting it behind them, regardless of whether it was satisfactory to the parties involved or not. The few times the police were brought to the school were basically to wag their fingers at the school to tell them to &quot;keep it down&quot;. People were rarely expelled and punishments weren't very punitive.<br /> <br /> I was bullied because of apathy on the part of the people in charge, and the lesson I learned from it was very much a basic &quot;Act or be Acted Upon&quot;. At the time, the line was &quot;Everyone is free to be who they are...&quot; but always underlined with &quot;...as long as it's socially acceptable and doesn't inconvenience someone&quot;. The bullying I received largely stopped when I started throwing punches and nothing was done to stop me, just as nothing was done to stop the people initially throwing punches at me. That's the lesson I learned, and as a result, as an adult, I react very negatively to snark, and &quot;cute&quot; sarcasm and prickishness. Sometimes that makes social situations a little rough, but it did teach me the value of self-agency. Mixed bag result!<br /> <br /> Now, having come to the other side of the experience as a teacher; the feel of a highschool (and schools in general) have very little to do with the students themselves and more with the pervasive attitude and feeling of &quot;safeness&quot; and &quot;connection&quot; the school environment itself entails. This goes for any school of adolescents, in America or in my experiences teaching abroad. So, Zid, my advice to you in portraying teenagers is consider the trickle-down effect of the environment in which they are being taught, then construct your median from there, and then create a few outliers and extreme-reactions to said environment. That will lend an authentic feel to the NPC's, I believe.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, play Rockstar's &quot;Bully&quot; for a great pulpy take on lighthearted high-school hijinks which you might be able to transfer into a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":255,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","user":"ParanoiaCombo","date":". 01-29-2014, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T07:08:08-08:00","id":60734,"title":"","content":"Wow! <br /> <br /> I fired this post off a while back, and I thought it had dwindled and died. Thanks for all the responses! I'd thank you all, but my 'like' clicker finger is about to become strained. I'm still in the process of designing this part of the campaign, by the way, so your input is still 'fresh' as it were. I've got about 2 pages to catch up on!<br /> <br /> <br /> Danke!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/219-zid","name":"Zid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T09:05:37-08:00","id":60822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=60700#post60700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bullying is a thing, but it's never at the Biff Tannen levels in real life.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have never been dragged through the men's locker room by your backpack then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T10:08:28-08:00","id":60879,"title":"","content":"I think that the reason bullying is so bad in American high schools doesn't really say much about American high schoolers so much as how terribly run, overcrowded, and prison-like the public schools are. When you treat kids like prisoners, I don't think it's that surprising that they start acting like prisoners do. That said, whenever I read these stories about extreme bullying, I can't help but react to them with the same level of discomfort that I would a graphic depiction of rape. I really, really hate that kids are subjected to this kind of treatment. My own school experiences had me mostly as the weird, awkward, and sometimes cringey kid who had a few friends but that most people ignored. In high school it got more dramatic as I got more opinionated and ornery, while simultaneously going through an oh-god-please-like-me phase, but high school was mostly something I just allowed to happen until I graduated while tuning out almost all of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When Heaven forbids Exigents, only forbidden gods will have Exigents. <b>The Hanged Man wrote:</b> Space. Pfft, whatever. I can kick Space's ass with a starting Dynast.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/716-capybara","name":"Capybara!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar716_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T13:55:35-08:00","id":61031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Sad Ghost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=59567#post59567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do people outside of the United States view bullying in schools? Is it a thing that happens often? Maybe you got lucky because you're Ottawasian. (I peeked at your profile to learn that because I am an ace internet sleuth)</div> </div> </div> </div>Going by my memory...<br /> <br /> We don't approve of bullying. I mean, who does?<br /> <br /> Sometimes school campaigns portray bullying as some kind of hideous crime comparable to genocide, but...advertising aimed at children is often over-the-top. (They don't actually say it's equal to genocide or anything, they just condemn it hyperbolically.)<br /> <br /> Anyway, my good experience might be because I'm not American. Or it might be because I went to a good high school or because I'm me. Who knows?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=60700#post60700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bullying is a thing, but it's never at the Biff Tannen levels in real life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure you're wrong about that. It doesn't pay to underestimate the human capacity for evil. Or the human capacity for good, to be fair, but that's off-topic.<br /> <br /> You might have an unrealistically rosy picture because you went to a good high school.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T14:18:40-08:00","id":61048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=60700#post60700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bullying is a thing, but it's never at the Biff Tannen levels in real life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bullying can end in murder and rape in real life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T14:44:58-08:00","id":61078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryumaru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=60567#post60567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything you see reported on in the news here? That's just the aftershow. High school in America is a fucking <i>microcosm</i> of what you see the news rant and rave about. All that abuse, mudslinging, horrendous behavior and miserable examples of human beings? Where the fuck do you think they learned that shit?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to make a quick addendum to this: Where do you think they learned <i>they can get away with it</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/2480852/chapters/5503997\" target=\"_blank\">Glorious Echeladder Ascension Technique</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/287292-glorious-echeladder-ascension-technique-a-homestuck-exalted-crossover\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Topic</a><br /> <br /> &quot;Look, sometimes you just are in the mood to play the divinely empowered champion of the God of Farts. Mechanically optimized play is not the only way to enjoy playing your character.&quot; -Wise Old Guru","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1048-ryumaru","name":"Ryumaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1048_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T14:49:54-08:00","id":61081,"title":"","content":"I posted a thing (in this thread), then I deleted it because I was like &quot;meh, nevermind, nobody cares anyway&quot; (ironic as that's one of the things bullying does to you -- self-dismissal). Is there a way to get it back? (at the time it said there was a way to undelete because it was a &quot;soft delete&quot; but I can't find the option anywhere)<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'll restart I guess. My life in high-school was comparable to being caged in with sharks or hyenas - they'd poke and nibble at you to test you out, and when you offered any resistance / fought back, that's when the real feeding frenzy would commence. Usually with you being outnumbered (they'd get you at times when you are alone, no matter how many friends you have.)<br /> <br /> Some excerpts of my school experience (Quebec, Canada) include the following (all day, every day, for 5 years):<br /> <br /> - Being called an ugly worthless gay weak idiot while being slammed into lockers and getting slapped upside the head.<br /> - Having rocks thrown at me by 5 guys that would follow me partway home most evenings and beat me if I would offer any resistance, just because they were bored.<br /> - The guy sitting in front of me would slam his chair into my desk, in turn slamming my desk into me. The guy behind me, his friend, would do the same with his desk.<br /> - Getting spitballs and erasers thrown at the back of my head (sometimes the teachers would get them too, when they weren't looking).<br /> - Just the never-ending stream of insults, of shoves, slaps, spits, etc. Every day for five years.<br /> (Not to mention the numerous times kids were busted for drugs (usually pot and mushrooms, but often ecstasy and lsd, rare times cocaine) and for hiding handguns in their lockers (once or twice).)<br /> <br /> Amongst other things. On top of that, adults (parents and friends' parents, not teachers) telling you to stop being such a girl, to suck it up and ignore them because they'll go away if they get no reaction (hint: no, not at all, not ever). They don't help you to deal with the sheer amount of fear, sadness and blind rage that it induces. They just tell you to ignore it, because if you do it'll go away.<br /> <br /> The only time those things subsided even a little is when I snapped and choked a guy halfway into unconsciousness (one of the chronic bullies), probably wouldn't have stopped until he was out cold if a teacher didn't pull me away.<br /> <br /> A lot of kids walk away from that pretty damaged later in their lives - trust issues, alcoholism, flashbacks that keep you up at night where you keep analyzing the situation, uncontrollable rage outbursts. Some people, now grown adults, can't even walk by a group of teenagers without feeling a rise of defensive adrenaline and hatred, as though they were about to get attacked.<br /> There were a couple studies that examined the phenomenon and found that it was remarkably similar to post-traumatic stress, from all the years of unrelenting abuse, similar to how soldiers would still expect aerial strikes or guerrilla squads to come get them even after the war they fought in long passed. (I'm not trying to say that it's exactly the same, clearly war veterans have it much, much rougher, but the phenomenon is similar.)<br /> <br /> If you had a horrible time in high-school and you've noticed you exhibit some of the things I mentioned above (mistrust, rage, paranoia), you're not crazy, it's a thing and it can be helped. Mostly just by talking about it to someone that cares (friends, family, significant others) and won't dismiss it as &quot;it's all in your head&quot;. Yes, it's in your head, and it won't go away. That's the problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 01-29-2014, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T14:54:56-08:00","id":61088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=61048#post61048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bullying can end in murder and rape in real life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T15:09:41-08:00","id":61101,"title":"","content":"One thing you need to realize about the American Public School system is that there is no such thing as the American Public School System.<br /> <br /> America is not a country, it is about, give or take, 50 different countries that more or less agreed to get along and is held together by spit and prayer.<br /> <br /> America is a <i>Federation</i>, and nearly every state is a power and culture upon itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T15:42:29-08:00","id":61122,"title":"","content":"What God_of_Awesome just said. America was founded on the ideals of Federalism, and while in many cases it could do better with a more centralized approach, the American public doesn't really trust the federal government to do anything right. What they don't realize is that the state governments aren't any better, and the states and feds playing hot potato with responsibilities is largely responsible for a lot of the bureaucratic mess that a lot of things are. Education included.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/673-requiem_jeer","name":"Requiem_Jeer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar673_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T15:53:04-08:00","id":61125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Requiem_Jeer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=61122#post61122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What God_of_Awesome just said. America was founded on the ideals of Federalism, and while in many cases it could do better with a more centralized approach, the American public doesn't really trust the federal government to do anything right. What they don't realize is that the state governments aren't any better, and the states and feds playing hot potato with responsibilities is largely responsible for a lot of the bureaucratic mess that a lot of things are. Education included.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we're drifting into politics, because I want to make a counterpoint about what you just said that would get me a mod warning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T16:07:07-08:00","id":61129,"title":"","content":"Whoops. Sorry mods!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/673-requiem_jeer","name":"Requiem_Jeer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar673_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T20:07:05-08:00","id":61261,"title":"","content":"My middle school years were horrendous, but by the time of high school things had evened out (for me). I was never one of the *popular* kids, but I joined the music and drama department early and had enough status as a hanger-on that I was mostly just ignored. <br /> <br /> Really, that was most of my experience for most of high school. I wasn't incredibly popular, but I wasn't *un*popular either. I didn't have the tormentors I'd had in earlier years, but I didn't have very many friends - at least, 'til senior year, when I joined the Sci Fi club and met the (essentially) family of friends I still carry to this day. <br /> <br /> Now, if you want to talk about junior high, *that* time sucked. I'd be clotheslined by two guys holding a backpack between them, or have someone pull on my own (heavy) backpack to knock me down. One time it was raining when I got to my bus stop, but the kid whose family owned that house refused to let me onto his porch, so I got soaked (as did everything in my backpack). That one, the teachers caught onto, though I didn't see any reprisal toward the other kid. <br /> <br /> Oddly enough, that's the one kid who came up to me years afterward (in high school, actually) to apologize for being horrible to me when we were younger. It's weird, just how good an apology can feel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T20:42:33-08:00","id":61280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=61048#post61048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bullying can end in murder and rape in real life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are crimes and can occur absent of bullying as well. Please respect goalposts where they're established.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T20:53:43-08:00","id":61286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=61280#post61280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are crimes and can occur absent of bullying as well. Please respect goalposts where they're established.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the goalposts you're moving? Because you said the following:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=60700#post60700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bullying is a thing, but it's never at the Biff Tannen levels in real life.</div> </div> </div> </div>One would assume, therefore, that pointing out that bullying can reach/exceed the levels of Biff Tannen would be applicable. Which is what hippokrene was doing. Unless you're saying that arguing against you is moving a goalpost, which would appear to be ludicrous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T22:47:12-08:00","id":61330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=61101#post61101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing you need to realize about the American Public School system is that there is no such thing as the American Public School System.<br /> <br /> America is not a country, it is about, give or take, 50 different countries that more or less agreed to get along and is held together by spit and prayer.<br /> <br /> America is a <i>Federation</i>, and nearly every state is a power and culture upon itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to get that granular (does granular mean more chunky or more powdery? I can never remember. I'm assuming it means more powdery), then the state level doesn't really matter either, and it's all about counties and cities and even then it's sort of a tossup. For example I live in Cook County, which covers all of Chicago and some of the surrounding towns and suburbs. Even if you ignore everything but Chicago, you cannot make any judgments about the quality of the local schools solely based on them being schools in Chicago. You can assume with statistical likelihood that the public schools are somewhere below average, because the CPS is a trainwreck, but your neighborhood and background can make the difference between going to an exceptional magnet school or a place where you may be safer leaving school and joining a gang (not hyperbole; very real problem).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When Heaven forbids Exigents, only forbidden gods will have Exigents. <b>The Hanged Man wrote:</b> Space. Pfft, whatever. I can kick Space's ass with a starting Dynast.","edited":{"userid":716,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/716-capybara","user":"Capybara!","date":". 01-30-2014, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/716-capybara","name":"Capybara!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar716_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T03:05:10-08:00","id":61427,"title":"","content":"Jesus H. Christ. The equivalent of high school here in Finland sounds like effing paradise after hearing the american stories. If anyone at my high school had repeatedly physically assaulted another student the teachers would have nuked them. Hell, if I recall correctly two junior high students fighting behind a gas station made it into a national news paper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1631-karthak","name":"Karthak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1631_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T06:28:37-08:00","id":61500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karthak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=61427#post61427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jesus H. Christ. The equivalent of high school here in Finland sounds like effing paradise after hearing the american stories. If anyone at my high school had repeatedly physically assaulted another student the teachers would have nuked them. Hell, if I recall correctly two junior high students fighting behind a gas station made it into a national news paper.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, it was like that over here in Germany, too. Except, you know, for those kids who're trouble anyway. They don't deserve/need justice/protection/help. It would be wasted effort anyway, obviously.<br /> Except for three teachers, who really tried to fight against the tide, to their great credit. But it was simply too much for them to keep an eye on everything and it's not like the bullies don't learn to wait for those few teachers to not be around.<br /> <br /> Although I should point out it's vastly different from school to school. I know people who wouldn't believe anything written in this thread, because of how good their school experience was, with competent and mostly impartial teachers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2UIUH9oaJnHMWIxcVdGMjNUYlE\" target=\"_blank\">3EX Martial Arts basic overview (Weapons, Armor, Attributes &amp; Abilities)</a>","edited":{"userid":366,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/366-edward-eldritch","user":"Edward Eldritch","date":".  EDIT: Forgot to finish a sentence. Presumptuous RL interefering with my posting. 01-30-2014, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/366-edward-eldritch","name":"Edward Eldritch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T07:28:03-08:00","id":61526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Capybara!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=61330#post61330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you want to get that granular (does granular mean more chunky or more powdery? I can never remember. I'm assuming it means more powdery), then the state level doesn't really matter either, and it's all about counties and cities and even then it's sort of a tossup. For example I live in Cook County, which is covers all of Chicago and some of the surrounding towns and suburbs. Even if you ignore everything but Chicago, you cannot make any judgments about the quality of the local schools solely based on them being schools in Chicago. You can assume with statistical likelihood that the public schools are somewhere below average, because the CPS is a trainwreck, but your neighborhood and background can make the difference between going to an exceptional magnet school or a place where you may be safer leaving school and joining a gang (not hyperbole; very real problem).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of the problem is that in American culture, not finishing high school is perceived as this giant social stigma and so no one will expel the bad kids from schools. I think if we decided that schools are for those that want to learn and threw out those who want to use it as a feeding ground to prey on other students, things would be better. Also, my high school diploma might be worth something more than just a &quot;you may now attend college&quot; ticket.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T09:03:37-08:00","id":61578,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure bullying isn't just a problem in the US. Kids being horribly mean to other kids seems to be a constant of human nature that appears everywhere from the Spartan Agoge to modern Korean and Japanese dramas. There are people in other countries that haven't experienced any bullying, just like there are people in the US who haven't experienced bullying. In fact, if you go to some of the schools described in this thread, you'll probably find plenty of people who didn't notice any bullying problem while they were there.<br /> <br /> My high school experience wasn't that bad. Despite being very socially awkward, I never had any trouble, possibly because the popular kids in my grade were genuinely nice people. Even one of the guys I had pinned as the &quot;bullying type&quot; (from a poorer background, smokes, drinks, cuts class etc.) helped me out on the side of the road when I had car troubles. There might have been bullying going on, but I might have been too busy being glad it wasn't me to pay much attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1970-yeangst","name":"yeangst","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T12:05:38-08:00","id":61660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=61526#post61526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think part of the problem is that in American culture, not finishing high school is perceived as this giant social stigma and so no one will expel the bad kids from schools. I think if we decided that schools are for those that want to learn and threw out those who want to use it as a feeding ground to prey on other students, things would be better. Also, my high school diploma might be worth something more than just a &quot;you may now attend college&quot; ticket.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm uncomfortable with the notion that kids can be branded &quot;bad&quot; and denied the right to an education. I think that if the school system was designed and run competently, you would very rarely run into cases where expelling a child would be an acceptable or reasonable solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When Heaven forbids Exigents, only forbidden gods will have Exigents. <b>The Hanged Man wrote:</b> Space. Pfft, whatever. I can kick Space's ass with a starting Dynast.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/716-capybara","name":"Capybara!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar716_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T13:12:23-08:00","id":61691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Capybara!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=61660#post61660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm uncomfortable with the notion that kids can be branded &quot;bad&quot; and denied the right to an education.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not, so much. I mean, certainly I would want there to be opportunity for more than one chance, and appropriate due process, but I think the pedestal upon which we have placed our children that basically affords them treatment superior to that of just about all other members of our society is a cultural sickness that has created many problems, including some mentioned in this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T13:39:47-08:00","id":61714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Capybara!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=61660#post61660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm uncomfortable with the notion that kids can be branded &quot;bad&quot; and denied the right to an education. I think that if the school system was designed and run competently, you would very rarely run into cases where expelling a child would be an acceptable or reasonable solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem isn't the school systems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T14:04:50-08:00","id":61734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yishten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=61691#post61691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm not, so much. I mean, certainly I would want there to be opportunity for more than one chance, and appropriate due process, but I think the pedestal upon which we have placed our children that basically affords them treatment superior to that of just about all other members of our society is a cultural sickness that has created many problems, including some mentioned in this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking about a placing kids on a pedestal. I consider an educational system that endemically produces disinterested or violent students to be one that has failed in its purpose. I think that the value placed on the Common Core to the exclusion of fundamental life skills like how to learn, reason, socialize, empathize, and pursue objectives is one that makes the current school system a relic of the Prussian education system. Children should be taught more-or-less the same way that adults are--with classes led by teachers who actually know what they're teaching, in a setting that allows for questions and dissent, and with a high degree of personal autonomy and the ability to create their own schedule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=61714#post61714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem isn't the school systems.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is the school systems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When Heaven forbids Exigents, only forbidden gods will have Exigents. <b>The Hanged Man wrote:</b> Space. Pfft, whatever. I can kick Space's ass with a starting Dynast.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/716-capybara","name":"Capybara!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar716_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T15:17:04-08:00","id":61770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=61714#post61714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem isn't the school systems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are...are you serious? There are many, many, many problems with the American Education system(really the only one I am familiar with). I'm not saying every school/School district is horrible, but there are ones that are, and most districts seem to be under quite a bit of pressure, and the only way they can see to solve the pressure is to make themselves measurably worse as schools.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that there aren't students who are a problem, but saying that the school system in America is flawless is like saying 2nd edition has a mechanically robust system, with special focus on Sidereals, and the wonderful flavor of Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T15:19:35-08:00","id":61772,"title":"","content":"The worst it <i>ever</i> really came to, for me, was when I received (pretty much false) accusations of harassment towards a few women, which caused me to get expelled a few times when I attempted to fight those accusations rather than just going with the flow. <br /> <br /> It was quite anger-inducing at the time, t'be honest. <br /> <br /> Beyond that...I was largely well-liked in Middle School, although I hardly interacted with anyone (nobody really shared my interests, so...what was I supposed to do?), due to a reputation for niceness and intelligence (and, to be totally honest, a bit of a physical attractiveness bump, I think. Cue the disagreement from people). Elementary school featured a few insults that went my way in first and second grade, but I largely brought those upon myself by deliberately annoying people.<br /> <br /> So...yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/781-chained-divinity","name":"Chained Divinity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar781_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T15:38:48-08:00","id":61786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Capybara!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=61660#post61660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm uncomfortable with the notion that kids can be branded &quot;bad&quot; and denied the right to an education. I think that if the school system was designed and run competently, you would very rarely run into cases where expelling a child would be an acceptable or reasonable solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm uncomfortable that I was verbally, emotionally, and physically assaulted by my peer group for twelve years with no personal recourse except to illegal violence, a recourse I was unwilling to take (I don't want to go to prison for murder).<br /> <br /> Gaining an education is not a right - a reasonable chance at an education is a right. Even if the school system wasn't bogged down with useless teachers (thanks teacher's union!), backlogged with useless litigation, and tied up in bureaucracy, you will still see kids who can not respect their peers rights to learn in a safe environment. Just as those who commit violent crimes are not allowed to walk around free, those that are actively detrimental to those around them in schools should not be allowed to remain. Otherwise, you're throwing piranha into a tank of goldfish and expecting them to play nice with each other.<br /> <br /> School discipline is toothless because they have nothing with which to threaten a bully. Suspensions are free holidays from school. Detention? Boring, but nothing earth-shattering. Expulsion is the only option schools have that actually hurts, if only they were willing to use it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=61714#post61714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem isn't the school systems.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you mean the problem of bad kids isn't caused by the school system, yes. Usually, bad kids are a product of poor parents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T16:19:41-08:00","id":61812,"title":"","content":"There are a couple of problems with the 'just kick out the bad ones' idea.<br /> <br /> 1) How 'bad' a student's actions are perceived depends on their race. There have been several studies that show when white students and black students engage in the same behavior, the black students are more likely to be labeled a problem.<br /> <br /> 2) Bad students are more likely to be from bad backgrounds. Taking a group of people with antisocial tendencies who are more likely to be suffering from abuse or poverty or other troubled home life and removing their ability to get basic math and writing skills is going to increase social stratification and the number of people who become criminals.<br /> <br /> 3) Bullying sometimes happens with the tact approval of teachers and other authority figures. Transgender students, for example, recieve all types of abuse that's ignore or condoned by teachers/principles; if said teacher or principle had the ability to remove troublemakers, it's very likely that the bullies would not be the ones kicked out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T18:14:38-08:00","id":61889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=61812#post61812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a couple of problems with the 'just kick out the bad ones' idea.<br /> <br /> 1) How 'bad' a student's actions are perceived depends on their race. There have been several studies that show when white students and black students engage in the same behavior, the black students are more likely to be labeled a problem.<br /> <br /> 2) Bad students are more likely to be from bad backgrounds. Taking a group of people with antisocial tendencies who are more likely to be suffering from abuse or poverty or other troubled home life and removing their ability to get basic math and writing skills is going to increase social stratification and the number of people who become criminals.<br /> <br /> 3) Bullying sometimes happens with the tact approval of teachers and other authority figures. Transgender students, for example, recieve all types of abuse that's ignore or condoned by teachers/principles; if said teacher or principle had the ability to remove troublemakers, it's very likely that the bullies would not be the ones kicked out.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are showing too much sympathy for the abuser. I will acknowledge that students who are expelled and do not have the self-discipline to read the writing on the wall and shape up are pretty much socially doomed. They will struggle through life, be more likely to have further social problems, and all the rest that goes with it.<br /> <br /> I'll still take that over letting what happened to me happen to another person and I think I got off easy. If I'd been gay, trans, disabled, or otherwise, I could very well have been beaten to death. If we cull those who are causing problems, perform some social triage and discard the ones who are unwilling to save themselves, then maybe people like me can get through school without having our normal emotional responses overridden by survival impulses. I can not get sad without feeling irrationally angry at everyone nearby, because tears got me picked on and blind rage occasionally won me some battles.<br /> <br /> Racism, sexism, and social stratification are not reasons for inaction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T18:31:43-08:00","id":61900,"title":"","content":"I've been watching this discussion and think it's moved away from a topic suitable for the Exalted forum.<br /> <br /> I'm open to suggestions, if people want to keep going I'd be happy to move it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T19:32:59-08:00","id":61935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=61900#post61900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been watching this discussion and think it's moved away from a topic suitable for the Exalted forum.<br /> <br /> I'm open to suggestions, if people want to keep going I'd be happy to move it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been trying to construct a response for some time now, so I'd be quite happy to finally make it on another section of the forum. XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/781-chained-divinity","name":"Chained Divinity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar781_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T21:03:20-08:00","id":61975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=61889#post61889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Racism, sexism, and social stratification are not reasons for inaction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps not inaction, but I'm not sure the given action you propose would help matters. I do think that the current system at best does nothing to bullies in the main, and possibly aides them (the persistent claim that suspensions are essentially vacations, which I have heard anecdotal support for but have not investigated).<br /> <br /> And the issue you sidestep in that last line is that your proposals would, essentially, emplace school administrations as empowered bullies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T22:07:36-08:00","id":61993,"title":"","content":"I expect that a &quot;just kick them out&quot; policy would frequently lead to the wrong person getting kicked out.<br /> <br /> Especially when you take racism and homophobia into account. Hypothetical gay black Kyeudo would be more likely to be expelled than his bullies would be. Actual straight white Kyeudo would have had better odds, but he'd still be at risk of expulsion.<br /> <br /> Pretty much all zero-tolerance policies that have been introduced so far have been utter failures, why should this one be any different?<br /> <br /> The best solution is simple but ridiculously difficult: hire good teachers/administrators and adjust society so that the students are better people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T22:10:10-08:00","id":61994,"title":"","content":"I come from Australia.<br /> <br /> I have learned one thing from my experiences, and that is appearances matter, because I was a fat nerd in primary school and the start of high school. My friends and I were bullied pretty harshly during those formative years. In a digital art class (basically, learning how to use Photoshop and other programs for artistic and editing purposes), there were a group of three guys who bullied a friend of mine relentlessly. I have no idea why these guys were in the class, because they didn't really participate in any of the lessons or finish their assignments.<br /> <br /> I recall the time my friend finally told one of the guys: &quot;Fuck off!&quot; The bully then stood up, grabbed his chair and belted my friend with the chair. My friend was badly hurt, went to hospital, and the guy was threatened with expulsion (although, he ended up only getting suspended and a bunch of detentions).<br /> <br /> After the fact, one of the other guys started 'bullying' me. Bullying seems like a non-word to me, really. Really, these guys were just awful people. I don't even remember one of their names. Anyway, the guy used to sit behind me and kick me in the back whenever he felt like it. The third guy was really nondescript and was more someone who was just around and laughed at this crap.<br /> <br /> After I finished that class, I never really saw these guys again, except it turned out the third guy was a mutual friend of one of mine. Weird. Never spoke to him, though, so whatever.<br /> <br /> Another time a guy was making fun of the way I spoke (I have asperger's, plus at the time a speech impediment), and I retaliated by telling the guy he was fat (I was still podgy, so in hindsight it's deliciously hypocritical)... not really bullying, so much as two guys butting heads... he hit me with his backpack, and he ended up getting litter duty. After the fact, we actually got along very well and I have to say he ended up being one of the nicest guys I knew in high school. Weird. But funny.<br /> <br /> Anyway, during mid-high school, I hit puberty proper... slimmed down, got taller, lost my speech impediment (learned to pretend to understand people), and things changed pretty quickly for me. Why? I was now good-looking, fortunate enough to have sisters who told me what was popular to wear, and started building up a lot of friends. Teachers liked me. I was a good kid and never got in trouble.<br /> <br /> I was and am very nerdy, but I didn't really look it in high school. (e.g. a sister's friend came over, and I greeted her politely, then went to another room. I overheard her telling my sister, &quot;I thought you said your brother was nerdy?&quot; And my sister saying, &quot;He is! I swear he is!&quot; -- I joke with my sister about this still and she says she was really weird in high school and doesn't know what she was thinking lol).<br /> <br /> Anyway, so I was mildly popular... but this is another thing that has stuck with me forever and I regret it a lot...<br /> <br /> I got asked out by a really mousy and nerdy girl; she was in my SOSE class and we never spoke before; she drew me a really nice picture to ask me out and in hindsight it was an incredibly nice gesture. I was sitting with friends and my friends took it from my hands. And they laughed. Made fun of it. And ripped it into pieces and it was clearly a horrible thing to do while she watched. I didn't rip it, but I did nothing to fix the situation. And I regret being a sheep and an utter coward for not doing anything helpful. She was very badly bullied. Eventually, the girl committed suicide about a year later. It's pretty much stayed with me forever and is a clear indicator that being a dick to people is really not okay and there can be awful ramifications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1592,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","user":"Jack","date":". 01-31-2014, 03:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T03:41:50-08:00","id":62070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=61812#post61812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a couple of problems with the 'just kick out the bad ones' idea.<br /> <br /> 1) How 'bad' a student's actions are perceived depends on their race. There have been several studies that show when white students and black students engage in the same behavior, the black students are more likely to be labeled a problem.<br /> <br /> 2) Bad students are more likely to be from bad backgrounds. Taking a group of people with antisocial tendencies who are more likely to be suffering from abuse or poverty or other troubled home life and removing their ability to get basic math and writing skills is going to increase social stratification and the number of people who become criminals.<br /> <br /> 3) Bullying sometimes happens with the tact approval of teachers and other authority figures. Transgender students, for example, recieve all types of abuse that's ignore or condoned by teachers/principles; if said teacher or principle had the ability to remove troublemakers, it's very likely that the bullies would not be the ones kicked out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to agree with everything hippokrene said. It's sad, but true.<br /> <br /> Over here in Germany, it's weird, regarding race. 90% of the time it doesn't matter at all, except for people annoyingly trying to be correct about it. But when it does crop up, it's obvious people either preferentially treat those of their race, or in some instances, do the exact opposite, just to not be racist. Add to that, that if you're even just a bit non-white, you just have to imply racism is part of the situation for every adult to freak out and try to make things right for you. Of course that's also racist, but it's not what people think of when you use that term. I think I haven't had any contact with what people traditionally call racism during my school time. I don't think I've even met someone who's been treated racist, ever. That changed after certain insane people with planes, but that I completely blame on the media and while it's affected my chances on the job-market, other than that I usually just have to patiently tell people they're being stupid and explain why I'm not a Muslim even though I'm half-arabic.<br /> <br /> If I had wanted to, I could easily have abused my &quot;race&quot; in school. I had to clear up multiple misunderstandings that led people to thinking something might have happened because of racism. When I did, any interest in my situation went away, which is the actual tragedy. My school was actually pretty quick to kick people out because of alleged racism, which certainly was unfounded in every case I know of and also didn't do those people any favors in becoming productive parts of society.<br /> <br /> We're lucky enough that there have been enough studies about this kind of thing, that we can be relatively certain that it just makes a bad situation worse if you kick people out who cause trouble. Because as hippokrene also pointed out, they usually have something bad going on at home, as well. And it easily hits the wrong people. I more or less had teachers gang up on me to make sure I'd fail one year, which in hindsight worked out very well for me, but it certainly wasn't intended to help me. If they could have, they'd have thrown me out of school right away. And that's simply because I questioned them and saw no reason to treat them with the degree of respect they expected from us students.<br /> <br /> Almost a decade after that crap happened to me, I got into a rather prestigious institution because I passed a &quot;gifted&quot; test. There I got to see how schools are supposed to be run. Every teacher there cared, save two, one who also wasn't good at her job and she was replaced within a month after we reported we weren't impressed with her as a teacher. The other was still an amazing teacher, so it was easy to accept that we had a single mostly uncaring educator.<br /> Anyone who got in trouble always could go to the educators or the headmaster for help, even regarding things not even related to the academy. There were a very few attempts at bullying. Those people that same day were sent to the headmaster and he talked to them, calmly explaining that opposed to regular schools, there would be consequences, including detailed reports to the people paying for their education. It was weird how quickly those people abandoned their previous behavior. And it took them a couple of weeks to find a new place in our class, but except for a single guy who was expelled because he never attended class, we all got along fine. Not necessarily great, but it was civilized.<br /> Three things were different in that place. Teachers cared and the academy had insane amounts of money it kept investing in projects to further improve the academy and we actually learned useful things there. Now, I need to stress that while the money certainly helped get the good teachers, other than that it was just a bonus. It wasn't required to improve the situation we're talking about.<br /> <br /> Now imagine I'd still be the same, basically nice, ages ago meek and shy guy I was and got kicked out but with no chance to get into such an institution? I'd have turned to crime or accepted drudge work. There's no question about it for me. And giving people the impression that their only choices are crime, being a failure or suicide is a really bad thing to do.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, there are people who deserve to be expelled, but it's almost certainly a very small amount of people. The sub-culture of school usually simply doesn't teach these people that their behavior is even wrong. Punishing them for making life hell for other students, without using it to communicate that message wouldn't achieve good things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2UIUH9oaJnHMWIxcVdGMjNUYlE\" target=\"_blank\">3EX Martial Arts basic overview (Weapons, Armor, Attributes &amp; Abilities)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/366-edward-eldritch","name":"Edward Eldritch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T05:15:38-08:00","id":62087,"title":"","content":"@Capybara: okay, I accept this proposal (while difficult to implement AT BEST) would likely help. <br /> <br /> But it won't eliminate all problems. As has been pointed out, bad parenting, at least , can also create problem students, and I, at least, don't exclude the possibility of just plain bad human beings (including kids-- one of the aspects of putting then on a pedestal is the idea, held by many that would otherwise wash their hands of an adult criminal, that juveniles are somehow different and incapable if being unworthy of society's efforts). What to do about them?<br /> <br /> @CoSaR and hippokrene: with appropriate due process, school administrators would be no more in a position to be approved bullies or to act on their personal &quot;-isms&quot; than the justice system is currently. Note that I recognize that the justice system certainly does not avoid these problems. But while many of us work to change the justice system, I think most of u also accept it's better than nothing in the meantime. Why, then, is doing nothing preferably to even a flawed system to root out and deal with serious student troublemakers? If it's a good enough system for the rest of us to work with for the moment, why isn't it a good enough system for our kids?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T07:54:21-08:00","id":62166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yishten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=62087#post62087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@CoSaR and hippokrene: with appropriate due process, school administrators would be no more in a position to be approved bullies or to act on their personal &quot;-isms&quot; than the justice system is currently. Note that I recognize that the justice system certainly does not avoid these problems. But while many of us work to change the justice system, I think most of u also accept it's better than nothing in the meantime. Why, then, is doing nothing preferably to even a flawed system to root out and deal with serious student troublemakers? If it's a good enough system for the rest of us to work with for the moment, why isn't it a good enough system for our kids?</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is that the 'appropriate due process' is basically what we have now. <br /> <br /> Also, nice strawman: I don't advocate doing nothing(as I explicitly said in my posts). But while doing nothing is not the best option, I don't think the proposed option would actually be better. So, no, I don't see any reason to make the situation worse, simply so that we can say we did something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T08:14:04-08:00","id":62181,"title":"","content":"I gotta say, I disapprove of the &quot;well some people are just bad so get rid of them&quot; sentiment as it pertains to education. <i>Especially</i> as it pertains to <i>education</i>.<br /> <br /> As much as I got shat on at school, I'm pretty sure expelling the shitters, while making the school <i>maybe</i> a better place, wouldn't have made <i>them</i> any better. It would just move the problem elsewhere, like out into the poor neighborhoods where people with no jobs end up dealing drugs to just barely pay next month's rent.<br /> <br /> Puberty being the (second) most important formative period in human life, it's more important to teach them to behave than to teach them that people will give up on them. Mainly because towards the end of puberty is when your personality stabilizes and most of who-you-will-be is formed. That's in part why the system must be different from the rest of the world - the rest of the world Isn't <i>teaching kids to become adults</i> (the education system might be failing at this point but that's a separate issue), it's dealing with adults that have already finished developing and have made their choices.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure (with nothing but anecdotal evidence, mind) that they too are succumbing to stress and pressures that come from outside of school (or maybe even others inside school), like from living with alcoholic, violent or overbearing parents (essentially being bullied by their parents), coping with the loss or the drug addiction of a family member etc; and that helping them deal with those stresses and pressures is more important than &quot;whatever, get out&quot;. Essentially, I'm suggesting that they don't know any better. They literally haven't learned how to deal with stress and how what they do impacts others. Ideally, parents should be teaching this, but parents are fallible human beings as well and tend to pass on their failures and biases as much as anything else.<br /> <br /> Hell, with all the research done into incentivizing behaviors in game systems (see casinos), that research would be put to good use in education (and other) systems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T08:55:01-08:00","id":62212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=61900#post61900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been watching this discussion and think it's moved away from a topic suitable for the Exalted forum.<br /> <br /> I'm open to suggestions, if people want to keep going I'd be happy to move it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shh shhh shhhhh.....<br /> <br /> This is healthy, it's part of the <i>healing</i>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T09:07:27-08:00","id":62218,"title":"","content":"@CoSaR: Insofar as I don't see any reason to expect doing anything else can solve the whole problem, your argument, to me, is de facto doing nothing. You can try to play word games til the cows come home, but unless you make a positive statement of what you do recommend doing that gives me reason to think it is (a) feasible and (b) would actually solve the problem, then to me your position is not meaningfully different than doing nothing. And whether or not there is currently adequate due process in place (arguable) is useless without teeth-- if you don't act, appropriately and meaningfully, on the result, then the trial was a waste of time. <br /> <br /> @Fata-Ku: I will modify my position a bit. I wouldn't advocate summary expulsion ever, and I'm not sure I'd advocate irrevocable expulsion for prepubescent kids either. I'll own that change though I'm not honestly sure the original proponent if the idea (Kyeudo, was it?) was advocating for anything pre-high school. <br /> <br /> But my willingness to accept &quot;society made me do it&quot; excuses only extends a very short distance. To do otherwise obliterates the value and correctness of those people dealt a shitty hand in life (and there are a lot of them) who don't go on to be fucking assholes. If you have two abused kids, and only one becomes a bully, the abuse serves as an explanation at best, not an excuse, because the other kid's not one. Same goes for criminals, whether they were expelled previously or not-- people need to be held accountable for their actions, adult or child (at least beyond a certain age or threshold of tolerability).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":926,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","user":"Yishten","date":". 01-31-2014, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T09:32:44-08:00","id":62239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yishten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=62218#post62218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@CoSaR: Insofar as I don't see any reason to expect doing anything else can solve the whole problem, your argument, to me, is de facto doing nothing. You can try to play word games til the cows come home, but unless you make a positive statement of what you do recommend doing that gives me reason to think it is (a) feasible and (b) would actually solve the problem, then to me your position is not meaningfully different than doing nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're saying that you won't accept criticism regarding a proposed solution for a problem unless someone proposes something better, and that you can't concieve of a better solution. Why enter the debate, then, if you are only going to spout off your ideas and insult others? Especially by out right misrepresenting what others say?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yishten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=62218#post62218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And whether or not there is currently adequate due process in place (arguable) is useless without teeth-- if you don't act, appropriately and meaningfully, on the result, then the trial was a waste of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like how you demand thought out strategies from others before they can even talk about the subject, and yet your own 'solution' is horribly thought out and contradictory. <br /> <br /> The schools currently have a system that uses due process: the issue is that due process makes things very, very difficult to prove, and thus nothing gets done. Usually, stuff like bullying can be very he said/she said, so the only way to implement your solution would be for administrators to either be able to expel without due process or to reverse the normal American ideas, and have people assumed to be guilty unless they can prove otherwise. Of course, this wouldn't solve things, for the simple reason that a bully could just accuse the other person. If it was actually implemented, I'd imagine that it would have to be something more like both the accuser and the accused are expelled (similar to how in some areas it doesn't matter who started a fight, both get punished equally). Granted, that might 'solve' the problem (for given values of solve), but it seems it would create many, many more problems, including the fact that the bullied aren't really being protected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T09:57:26-08:00","id":62263,"title":"","content":"I don't necessarily demand thoroughly thought out solutions. I do expect more than &quot;oh I think something should be done, but definitely not that&quot; without any effort to suggest what that &quot;something&quot; should be. You may disagree with a proposed solution and believe you've made some kind of adequate case for why it's a bad one, but at least it's a solution on the table, and you haven't made much of a case that it's bad other than to suggest school administrators would become bullies with more authority. <br /> <br /> Now, I am sorry if you feel insulted. I think your views are misguided and I think you have failed to offer any alternate solution, which I think is a default to the status quo, and which I think is de facto an argument in favor of doing nothing, but I mean no insult to you as a person. <br /> <br /> Finally, with respect, though proof can be a burden, it's not the problem. I have first hand and second hand knowledge of multiple instances of fully proven misbehavior on the part of students in 4 different US school systems. Despite such proof, the school systems (often at local or state government pressure) have a policy that expulsions are an admission of failure and to be avoided. So those students persist in the system. Teachers and administrators (inappropriately) stop trying to deal with most misbehavior because nothing comes of it, and it all gets worse. I also have first and secondhand knowledge of one US school system with a stricter policy and FAR fewer problems. I am personally aware and fully satisfied that such changes can benefit the school system, and for reasons I've pointed out, am not as concerned about the individuals expelled who failed to behave appropriately. So I have yet to hear a good argument to convince me otherwise, or a good alternative that might be expected to even do as much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":926,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","user":"Yishten","date":".  Typos 01-31-2014, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T10:57:03-08:00","id":62311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yishten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=62263#post62263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't necessarily demand thoroughly thought out solutions. I do expect more than &quot;oh I think something should be done, but definitely not that&quot; without any effort to suggest what that &quot;something&quot; should be. You may disagree with a proposed solution and believe you've made some kind of adequate case for why it's a bad one, but at least it's a solution on the table, and you haven't made much of a case that it's bad other than to suggest school administrators would become bullies with more authority.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, any idea is better than nothing. That seems very misguided, as it would mean that suggesting that all bullies be executed at the first accusation of bullying would be better than the status quo.<br /> <br /> Moreover, you're saying that no one can criticize and idea without first putting forward a solution, which is saying that you shouldn't bring up problems unless you personally have a solution to them, which I view as a horrible idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yishten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=62263#post62263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I am sorry if you feel insulted. I think your views are misguided and I think you have failed to offer any alternate solution, which I think is a default to the status quo, and which I think is de facto an argument in favor of doing nothing, but I mean no insult to you as a person.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you don't think it's a personal insult to be labeled as in favor of bullies when you merely don't think a given idea is a good one. Well, nice to have confirmation that you're entirely unreasonable and seemingly don't understand how ideas or criticism works. <br /> <br /> Hint: not all ideas are good ones.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yishten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=62263#post62263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, with respect, though proof can be a burden, it's not the problem. I have first hand and second hand knowledge of multiple instances of fully proven misbehavior on the part of students in 4 different US school systems. Despite such proof, the school systems (often at local or state government pressure) have a policy that expulsions are an admission of failure and to be avoided. So those students persist in the system. Teachers and administrators (inappropriately) stop trying to deal with most misbehavior because nothing comes of it, and it all gets worse. I also have first and secondhand knowledge of one US school system with a stricter policy and FAR fewer problems. I am personally aware and fully satisfied that such changes can benefit the school system, and for reasons I've pointed out, am not as concerned about the individuals expelled who failed to behave appropriately. So I have yet to hear a good argument to convince me otherwise, or a good alternative that might be expected to even do as much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? You know of a district that expels all bullies at the first sign of trouble with no possible recourse? Because that's what you seem to be defending(given that's what I was saying would be a bad idea).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T06:52:09-08:00","id":62882,"title":"","content":"Interesting thread...When I was in high school, there wasn't much of a problem with bullies. The school was more or less a refuge from other elements, and anyone who tried playing the bully was typically dealt with by other students. With extreme prejudice.<br /> These days the term &quot;zero tolerance&quot; is thrown about. And students need to know what that means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T08:55:49-08:00","id":62922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=62882#post62882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting thread...When I was in high school, there wasn't much of a problem with bullies. The school was more or less a refuge from other elements, and anyone who tried playing the bully was typically dealt with by other students. With extreme prejudice.<br /> These days the term &quot;zero tolerance&quot; is thrown about. And students need to know what that means.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that getting into a heated argument in public or having a utility knife will get the rest of your life ruined. <br /> <br /> Obey the rules, one mistake and your life is ruined.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T09:14:05-08:00","id":62929,"title":"","content":"Let's also not forget that &quot;zero tolerance&quot; has led schools to confiscate medication from students and suspend/expel them. A teenager has pills! They can't be having cramps or a headache, and definitely nothing more serious! They must be a drug addict! /s","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T09:46:33-08:00","id":62952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cielle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=62929#post62929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's also not forget that &quot;zero tolerance&quot; has led schools to confiscate medication from students and suspend/expel them. A teenager has pills! They can't be having cramps or a headache, and definitely nothing more serious! They must be a drug addict! /s</div> </div> </div> </div>*and* that such policies cut both ways.<br /> <br /> A teacher that finds even prescription medication on a student under zero tolerance and fails to report it faces penalties up to and including being dismissed with cause... which means they can pretty much kiss years of education and experience in teaching bye-bye because they're never going to get a job anywhere that's not desperate.<br /> <br /> So it's a situation in which the teachers have reason to NEVER make a judgement call, and one that encourages teachers specifically to NEVER investigate because it's either going to result in a student getting kicked out or themselves.<br /> <br /> So much for the idea of teachers being roll-models or trying to influence kids for the better, they now have good reason to make sure they're always as absolutely uninvolved as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T11:57:55-08:00","id":63034,"title":"","content":"Most parents know beforehand that they have to communicate any medical problems with the school before their child attend to begin with. Any parent that stupid not to know...makes me reconsider the validity of eugenics.<br /> And if there's a school without any form of nurse/doctor in it, is a school that isn't legitimate in any state.<br /> <br /> Lot of hyperbole being thrown in this thread. How can anyone take that seriously?<br /> <br /> I had some damn good teachers in high school.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T12:39:54-08:00","id":63054,"title":"","content":"In High School, and the preceding grade schools, my medical and psychiatric issues were constantly being misconstrued as bad behavior or insubordination precisely because the school was understaffed, underfunded and unprepared to deal with sick students.<br /> \u200bAs an example, I fell off the front of the stage while making my way to the wings (it was dark) after a theater class, and, after a very helpful peer (literally the only helpful thing that ass**** ever did For me and not To me) let me lean on them enough to limp to the nurse's office, the nurse turned out to be much more concerned about my WEIGHT and why I was late to class. She completely ignored my very obviously sprained ankle, which I repeatedly told her had a steel plate in it, explaining my concerns and level of pain. Simply ignored it.<br /> I can't think of one (out of literally thousands) &quot;behavioral incident&quot; in school involving me that can't, in hindsight, be explained by mental illness instead of simple unwillingness to behave. I got into fights often, because I was told by my dad that self-defense was always the solution to bullying. Of course, that meant multiple visits to the Principal's office for me. I would have days where my emotions were wildly unstable, often having a full-blown meltdown in class or in the schoolyard, leading to further reprimanded. Harming myself was the same thing, &quot;Stop doing that. We will not tolerate any such attention seeking behavior&quot;. They seriously did use the words &quot;attention-seeking&quot; many times.<br /> I was labeled a Bad Kid, while simultaneously being lauded as &quot;gifted&quot; due to high (and completely meaningless) scores on standardized tests. Apparently, one can be both a friendless nerd and a troublesome miscreant at the same time.* <br /> \u200b*So far, this dual-identities hall-pass is only a side effect of a broken educational system, and not a sweet Merit you can buy during High School Character Creation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 02-01-2014, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T12:44:52-08:00","id":63057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=63034#post63034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most parents know beforehand that they have to communicate any medical problems with the school before their child attend to begin with. Any parent that stupid not to know...makes me reconsider the validity of eugenics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good to know you promote eugenics as a solution. <br /> <br /> However zero tolerance is ZERO tolerance. There have been several cases of required prescription medication being taken away due to a form not being found. Note that doesn't mean that the paperwork wasn't files, that it couldn't be found. Investigations have concluded that the teaching staff behaved correctly. Which is why parents sue the board to change the policies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=63034#post63034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if there's a school without any form of nurse/doctor in it, is a school that isn't legitimate in any state.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it turns out you are flat out wrong. Nursing staff requirements are set at the state and county level and are highly variable.<br /> <br /> But hey, clearly the former wouldn't happen if the latter was true. <a href=\"http://www.rawstory.com/rs/2012/05/23/student-having-asthma-attack-denied-inhaler-by-school-nurse\" target=\"_blank\">Oh wait, it does.</a> Any reasonable person (and even the TSA) would note that the prescription is for the person in front of you and let them have it. But that violates school policy and thus is forbidden. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=63034#post63034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lot of hyperbole being thrown in this thread. How can anyone take that seriously?<br /> <br /> I had some damn good teachers in high school.</div> </div> </div> </div>How can anyone take it seriously when someone claims to have some damned good teachers and they fail to do even a basic check like &quot;I remember a nurse in my school, is that required everywhere?&quot;<br /> <br /> As for it being a one-shot ruin-your-life thing... let's pick something still hopeful... <a href=\"http://blog.heritage.org/2013/10/07/fishing-as-a-felony-teen-faces-prison-time-for-leaving-fishing-equipment-in-high-school-parking-lot/\" target=\"_blank\">here we go</a>. Parking at school with a short knife in a tackle-box is a federal crime. Clearly a 17 year old should know better than to make the mistake of not unloading his truck and making it school-safe. Why he should be happy that he's only likely to get 2 years in jail for this terrible crime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T13:57:38-08:00","id":63100,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=63057#post63057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div c