t63100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Variable doesn't mean nonexistent. Every school has to meet a certain requirement. Or are you going to attempt to say that there are schools with absolutely no policy regarding medical concerns whatsoever? Think about that for a second; A parent would have to be pretty damn moronic to send a child to such a school. And that's not even going into potential liability issues.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes and that minimum legal requirement is having a person and chain of redundancy for when that person is absent to call for appropriate emergency medical staff. In other words, the only medical requirement is being able to say that you have a policy that the principal will be the one to call 911 in an emergency.<br /> <br /> As for what you're supposed to do if you don't think a school district meets your requirements, it's great that you're convinced everyone is rich enough to be able to move school districts on a whim to ensure kids get increased supervision, but the reality is that most people can't afford to relocate or home school their children.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=63100#post63100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh great...a libertarian website...really? You'll find plenty of examples on such sites...whether there's truth...from your link: <i>If the district attorney decides to prosecute...</i>..Which apparently wasn't the case since <a href=\"http://www.examiner.com/article/felony-charges-to-be-dismissed-for-lassiter-high-school-student\" target=\"_blank\">the charges have been dropped</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, which is why I said I was using a hopeful example. The libertarian website as you kindly demean was the only one to actually mention it was a POSSIBILITY of charges rather than an absolute.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=63100#post63100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you're right. One shot can ruin your life:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://media-cache-ec0.pinimg.com/736x/7d/2f/0f/7d2f0f093ebf64d1f94c8f501c9827f6.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> Unfortunate that there are reasons for metal detectors in schools.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because people bring guns into schools and shoot people is a reason to deny medication and kick students out for having a pocketknife? And it's really amazing you know, the massive zero tolerance policies and somehow, magically, the mentally ill are still shooting up places. Amazing, don't these crazy criminals know it's against policy to bring a gun onto the property and face federal charges for doing so? Why you'd almost think that someone who has decided that shooting a bunch of children and teachers is a good idea somehow doesn't care about spending 2 years in jail for board of education violation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T19:08:28-08:00","id":63227,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=63144#post63144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah so you promote eugenics based on intelligence alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that such folks are Darwin Award winners.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=63144#post63144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Millions of what? People not stabbed to death with pocket knives? Feel free to drag up the statistics on how there were massive deaths in schools from medication abuse and pocket knives before zero tolerance was dreamed up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your too full of hyperbole, and not enough facts. Pocket knives are still considered weapons. Utility knives the same. Anyone smart enough to know how much damage a single razor can do knows this. (9/11 mean anything to you? How did they take control of those airplanes?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=63144#post63144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for what you're supposed to do if you don't think a school district meets your requirements, it's great that you're convinced everyone is rich enough to be able to move school districts on a whim to ensure kids get increased supervision, but the reality is that most people can't afford to relocate or home school their children.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, a lot of people do have children without giving any thought to schooling later on...<br /> I had several choices of public high schools. One was a 10 minute walk. The farthest was almost an hour walk. That was the safest one, and the one I chose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=63144#post63144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, which is why I said I was using a hopeful example. The libertarian website as you kindly demean was the only one to actually mention it was a POSSIBILITY of charges rather than an absolute.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think if you were to actually do a little more work, you'd find that common sense tends to be the rule rather than the exception when it comes to such things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=63144#post63144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because people bring guns into schools and shoot people is a reason to deny medication and kick students out for having a pocketknife</div> </div> </div> </div>If you've stats that show just how often meds are denied to those that need them while in school (like some diabetics for example) then show them. Because all I've ever heard were several silly examples that got a lot of media attention....and that was all. Logic says if it were common enough, there'd be lawsuits all over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T19:52:06-08:00","id":63701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=63227#post63227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure that such folks are Darwin Award winners.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your opinion, your right. While others may be delighted to see you keeping the spirit of Gesetz zur Verh\u00fctung erbkranken Nachwuchses alive and well, I for one am not. On that we'll have to simply disagree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=63227#post63227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your too full of hyperbole, and not enough facts. Pocket knives are still considered weapons. Utility knives the same. Anyone smart enough to know how much damage a single razor can do knows this. (9/11 mean anything to you? How did they take control of those airplanes?)</div> </div> </div> </div>With box razors of course. Anything can be turned into a weapon. Pocket knives, pens, pencils, paper and water, books... That's the whole point. You can't remove 100% of the things that can be used as weapons. Ever. I find it highly interesting that you apparently consider schools to be full of terrorists by dragging terrorist attacks into a discussion on schooling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=63227#post63227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, a lot of people do have children without giving any thought to schooling later on...<br /> I had several choices of public high schools. One was a 10 minute walk. The farthest was almost an hour walk. That was the safest one, and the one I chose.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm delighted for you. Most people don't live on the border of school districts or can afford to ship their children out of state because the state's policies don't meet increased requirements.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=63227#post63227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think if you were to actually do a little more work, you'd find that common sense tends to be the rule rather than the exception when it comes to such things.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's rather the whole point of Zero Tolerance. Teachers and staff are not permitted to apply opinions on board policy, it's a violation and grounds for dismissal. That's why so many teachers, parents and even politicians are driving to *remove* zero tolerance policies and replace them with the judgement calls on the part of educators that existed before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=63227#post63227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you've stats that show just how often meds are denied to those that need them while in school (like some diabetics for example) then show them. Because all I've ever heard were several silly examples that got a lot of media attention....and that was all. Logic says if it were common enough, there'd be lawsuits all over.</div> </div> </div> </div>Take it as a given that they are few and far between. Now provide any sort of evidence that Zero Tolerance policies have successfully prevented some horrific event or events that outweigh those few incidents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T20:53:07-08:00","id":63736,"title":"","content":"A bit late to this but here's my two cents. If I'm retreading over previously talked about material than I apologize.<br /> <br /> I've recently run a W20 game about high school students so I have a bit of experience with this kind of game. When I was doing it I tried focus more on the isolation and the unknown, the local Garou were preoccupied elsewhere, leaving them adrift to figure out their true nature, the real world around them and everything else on their own. With your idea it's much the same expect in all likelihood they are among the first of the DB so they won't have someone eventually come and help them make sense of it all. Nor would they have people who know about the dangers of the WoD so things would be a lot harder for them. Some of the ideas and material from Hunter: the Reckoning would do well here for that.<br /> <br /> Of course I wouldn't involve other supernaturals and the like right off the bat, allowing the PCs to start to get a feel for things and think that they understand the world only to get the surprise that there are other things out there, especially if you haven't told them about the CWoD aspects.<br /> <br /> Though I have to admit I'm not sure how things would translate between worlds. Even the DB are kind of overpowered compared to most average WoD supernaturals. Unless you're going to reduce or increase the power levels of one.<br /> <br /> One thing I would recommend taking a look at is <a href=\"http://parahumans.wordpress.com/about/\" target=\"_blank\">Worm</a>, a web serial set in an alternate Earth where in the 80's people spontaneously started gaining super powers. Fast-forward to today and parahumans are everywhere with some as Super Heroes but more as Super Villains, giant unkillable monsters periodically stomping through the place*, hidden conspiracies scheming, characters with hax powers, etc. Oh and the source of the parahuman powers sounds a lot like the Exalted Shards.<br /> <br /> *And when I say stomping through the place I would liken it to back when the Primordials would periodically stomp around Creation. Seriously by the time the story starts the monsters had already destroyed the islands of Japan and Newfoundland during their rampages.<br /> <br /> Anyway the story revolves around Taylor Hebert, a fifteen year old girl who is... well the definition of an outcast, tormented regularly by a trio of girls until one day they pull a especially traumatic prank** on her and that event causes her to trigger, gaining super powers. And while I haven't yet finished the story it reminds me some of the ideas and themes in WoD/CWoD lines and Exalted. It would actually make for a great alternate setting for said games. With your game it would make for an excellent possible future for the world with DB taking the place of the parahumans, depending of course on how the PCs act.<br /> <br /> **I use prank in the loosest terms here cause what they actually do is <i>really </i>horrible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T05:47:22-08:00","id":63899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=63701#post63701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With box razors of course. Anything can be turned into a weapon. Pocket knives, pens, pencils, paper and water, books... That's the whole point. You can't remove 100% of the things that can be used as weapons. Ever. I find it highly interesting that you apparently consider schools to be full of terrorists by dragging terrorist attacks into a discussion on schooling.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. There goes your hyperbole again. If knives aren't allowed (a demonstrative weapon) then lets turn everything into weapons. Or lets go in the other direction of hyperbole...and allow guns into schools too. See how that doesn't work? It seems you have particular with the middle ground.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=63701#post63701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm delighted for you. Most people don't live on the border of school districts or can afford to ship their children out of state because the state's policies don't meet increased requirements.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't speak for anyone but yourself. Period.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=63701#post63701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's rather the whole point of Zero Tolerance. Teachers and staff are not permitted to apply opinions on board policy, it's a violation and grounds for dismissal. That's why so many teachers, parents and even politicians are driving to *remove* zero tolerance policies and replace them with the judgement calls on the part of educators that existed before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um..yeah...These days Zero Tolerance policies aren't &quot;one size fits all.&quot; There's only one federal law that is mandated &quot;Zero Tolerance,&quot; and that deals with bringing a gun to school. And if you've a problem with that...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=63701#post63701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take it as a given that they are few and far between. Now provide any sort of evidence that Zero Tolerance policies have successfully prevented some horrific event or events that outweigh those few incidents.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think you can take it as a given that metal detectors prevented some teenage hijinks involving firearms. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T06:51:45-08:00","id":63939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=63899#post63899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. There goes your hyperbole again. If knives aren't allowed (a demonstrative weapon) then lets turn everything into weapons. Or lets go in the other direction of hyperbole...and allow guns into schools too. See how that doesn't work? It seems you have particular with the middle ground.<br /> <br /> You don't speak for anyone but yourself. Period.<br /> <br /> Um..yeah...These days Zero Tolerance policies aren't &quot;one size fits all.&quot; There's only one federal law that is mandated &quot;Zero Tolerance,&quot; and that deals with bringing a gun to school. And if you've a problem with that...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I think you can take it as a given that metal detectors prevented some teenage hijinks involving firearms. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>No. Zero Tolerance as a term is <b>defined</b> by a <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">strict and uncompromising application of the law, which forbids</span></span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"> persons in positions of authority from exercising discretion or changing punishments to fit the circumstances subjectively. Punishments are pre-determined and meted out regardless of extenuating circumstances or history. Zero Tolerance policies can only be &quot;one size fits all,&quot; as that is what the term means; what you are saying is a misnomer, or maybe an oxymoron. &quot;Zero Tolerance policy&quot; and &quot;discretion&quot; are incompatible terms.<br /> <br /> If you read the below link, the American Bar Assocation (ABA) even concludes &quot;</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">that such &quot;one-size-fits-all&quot; policies violate students' </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">due process</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> rights.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">reference: </span></span>http://legal-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/Zero+Tolerance","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1592,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","user":"Jack","date":". 02-03-2014, 09:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T06:56:42-08:00","id":63947,"title":"","content":"Out of the people I know, at most 20% are/were in a situation to choose schools.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I have trouble finding the right words without being insulting. The thought that anyone might actually believe metal detectors and insane security measures are a better investment than creating a better school environment is sheer madness to me.<br /> You can't stop a lone gunman. That will not change in the foreseeable future.<br /> You might be able to stop future lone gunmen from occurring.<br /> <br /> On another note, I'm getting the feeling from this and other places I visit that hyperbole is the new &quot;the nazis did that, too!&quot; of the internet. Anyone happen to know what made this so popular and widespread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2UIUH9oaJnHMWIxcVdGMjNUYlE\" target=\"_blank\">3EX Martial Arts basic overview (Weapons, Armor, Attributes &amp; Abilities)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/366-edward-eldritch","name":"Edward Eldritch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T08:01:44-08:00","id":63987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=63899#post63899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you can take it as a given that metal detectors prevented some teenage hijinks involving firearms. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Which is not a zero tolerance policy. <br /> <br /> Still waiting on any evidence that the increase from sane judgement based weapons policies to zero tolerance policies has in any way prevented shootings or other significant issues in schools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T12:18:05-08:00","id":64198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. Zero Tolerance as a term is defined by a strict and uncompromising application of the law, which forbids persons in positions of authority from exercising discretion or changing punishments to fit the circumstances subjectively. Punishments are pre-determined and meted out regardless of extenuating circumstances or history. Zero Tolerance policies can only be &quot;one size fits all,&quot; as that is what the term means; what you are saying is a misnomer, or maybe an oxymoron. &quot;Zero Tolerance policy&quot; and &quot;discretion&quot; are incompatible terms. If you read the below link, the American Bar Assocation (ABA) even concludes &quot;that such &quot;one-size-fits-all&quot; policies violate students' due process rights.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Again hyperbole. Were you to simply go into a school you'd find that teacher and staff exercise discretion every day. If that weren't the case, show me the stats of all the lawsuits being filed. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ed Eldritch</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thought that anyone might actually believe metal detectors and insane security measures are a better investment than creating a better school environment is sheer madness to me.</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;Better school environment&quot; How does that work in an urban school? One of the high schools I had a choice in going to, a teenage lass was raped while class was not only in session, but the teacher was standing not 20 feet away. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is not a zero tolerance policy.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's federal law. What would you call it? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still waiting on any evidence that the increase from sane judgement based weapons policies to zero tolerance policies has in any way prevented shootings or other significant issues in schools.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep waiting..You never gave me any stats showing anything that supported your claims. Which just tells me that's all they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"k