ls me that's all they are.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://lmgtfy.com/?q=define%3A+zero+tolerance\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://lmgtfy.com/assets/logo-color-small-d0f5c47d2b3adccd1be692d43c238d16961cb63d41b4a53c05f3f5b80d856699.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://lmgtfy.com/?q=define%3A+zero+tolerance\" target=\"_blank\"> LMGTFY </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://lmgtfy.com/?q=define%3A+zero+tolerance\" target=\"_blank\"> http://lmgtfy.com/?q=define%3A+zero+tolerance </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Let Me Google That For You (LMGTFY): for all those people who find it more convenient to bother you with their question rather than search it for themselves. </div> </div> </div><br /> Notice the lack of words that you keep using like &quot;federal law&quot;<br /> <br /> If you're going to keep throwing around a term and declaring that it's the greatest thing, learn what it means please.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=64198#post64198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You never gave me any stats showing anything that supported your claims. Which just tells me that's all they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so we agree to accept something (that incidents have occurred) and then you demand I show you stats that they have occurred?<br /> <br /> \u200bI think it's more a case that you *can't* prove Zero Tolerance does anything positive, because I've searched and can't find it. And now you're trying to pull a rather pathetic debate trick of going &quot;ummm, well you didn't prove this other stuff that we agreed on, so nyahh!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T12:46:59-08:00","id":64226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gee, sounds like everyone in that school should have up and moved to the next district with proper health and safety support. Good thing everyone had the option of doing just that.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's Camden NJ. The option that's usually chosen is simply not attend school. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Notice the lack of words that you keep using like &quot;federal law&quot; If you're going to keep throwing around a term and declaring that it's the greatest thing, learn what it means please.</div> </div> </div> </div> I just keep noticing the amazing lack of substance in your post. Or did you imagine that guns were ok? (Yes or no) <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so we agree to accept something (that incidents have occurred) and then you demand I show you stats that they have occurred?</div> </div> </div> </div> You first stated that I should simply take your word. But facts should be the rule. Not opinion. To repeat my inquiry; <i>If you've stats that show just how often meds are denied to those that need them while in school (like some diabetics for example) then show them. </i> But are you claiming that Zero Tolerance against guns in school accomplish nothing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T12:52:35-08:00","id":64234,"title":"","content":"Hey now, look at that; <a href=\"http://www.bloomberg.com/news/2014-02-03/is-school-shooting-a-wake-up-call-for-russia-.html\" target=\"_blank\">School Shooting in Russia</a> Interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T13:01:03-08:00","id":64243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=64226#post64226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just keep noticing the amazing lack of substance in your post. Or did you imagine that guns were ok? (Yes or no)</div> </div> </div> </div>That amusing, I (and apparently others) keep noticing the lack of research or thought in yours. <br /> <br /> Guns are irrelevant. Personally I don't think they should be permitted in schools since you want an answer.<br /> <br /> Now back to the actual topic of zero tolerance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=64226#post64226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You first stated that I should simply take your word. But facts should be the rule. Not opinion. To repeat my inquiry; <i>If you've stats that show just how often meds are denied to those that need them while in school (like some diabetics for example) then show them. </i> But are you claiming that Zero Tolerance against guns in school accomplish nothing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Incorrect. You stated that incidents where students were harmed by zero tolerance policies were few. I agreed and proceeded from that assumption you provided. I then challenged you to provide ANY evidence that zero tolerance polices were more effective than previous weapons policies on preventing violence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Originally posted by <b>Shadowflame</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=63227#post63227\">View Post</a></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">If you've stats that show just how often meds are denied to those that need them while in school (like some diabetics for example) then show them. Because all I've ever heard were several silly examples that got a lot of media attention....and that was all. Logic says if it were common enough, there'd be lawsuits all over.<br /> <br /> Take it as a given that they are few and far between. Now provide any sort of evidence that Zero Tolerance policies have successfully prevented some horrific event or events that outweigh those few incidents.</span></span></i></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> </span><br /> </i></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T23:29:58-08:00","id":64633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=64198#post64198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Again <b>hyperbole</b>. Were you to simply go into a school you'd find that teacher and staff exercise discretion every day. If that weren't the case, show me the stats of all the lawsuits being filed.</div> </div> </div> </div>see link for 'hyperbole': <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G2y8Sx4B2Sk\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G2y8Sx4B2Sk</a><br /> <br /> I gave the literal definition of Zero Tolerance. It is <i>inconceivable</i> that the literal definition of a term can be considered hyperbole or exaggeration. Moreover, I have a good hunch this disagreement stems from your misunderstanding of the philosophy behind Zero Tolerance. Zero Tolerance &quot;is defined by a strict and uncompromising application of the law, which forbids persons in positions of authority from exercising discretion or changing punishments to fit the circumstances subjectively.&quot; It is not a Zero Tolerance policy if teachers are exercising discretion.<br /> <br /> If you are fine with teachers using discretion, you are advocating something different to Zero Tolerance and this is a misnomer on your part. Plain and simple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1592,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","user":"Jack","date":". 02-04-2014, 02:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T23:37:08-08:00","id":64641,"title":"","content":"I can't be bothered to argue this out properly, but...Shadowflame, I disagree with you strongly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T07:02:13-08:00","id":64810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=64243#post64243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That amusing, I (and apparently others) keep noticing the lack of research or thought in yours.</div> </div> </div> </div>I only returned to you what you gave me. If you have stats from a pertinent agency then show them. Don't ask of others what you clearly won't do yourself.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=64243#post64243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guns are irrelevant. Personally I don't think they should be permitted in schools since you want an answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hate to break it to you, but guns are lumped into the whole &quot;Zero Tolerance&quot; thing. After all there are two categories regarding it and one of them is guns. The other is drugs.<br /> Things have dropped a bit since such policies have been adopted: <img src=\"http://www.drugabuse.gov/sites/default/files/styles/content_image_landscape/public/pastyearusealldrugs.jpeg?itok=1xh2T850\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Is it because of such policies? Regardless, Responsible parents want a safe environment for their children. An environment where teachers can maintain order. Difficult in an urban school which is something I'm pretty sure no one in this thread knows much about. But everyone hears plenty about school shootings in rural and suburban areas, where that sort of thing tends to happen the most.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=64633#post64633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">see link for 'hyperbole': <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G2y8Sx4B2Sk\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G2y8Sx4B2Sk</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't do youtube, especially when someone can't properly argue the point himself. (But I suppose that's an opinion.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=64633#post64633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are fine with teachers using discretion, you are advocating something different to Zero Tolerance and this is a misnomer on your part. Plain and simple.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it seems to me that is what we have today; discretion. As long as it doesn't endanger funding (Federal law) that is what's going on today.<br /> Yes, there seems to be the relative few that gets the media parade. But out of thousands of schools, typically laughed off as rural backwards localities.<br /> <br /> I should hope that common sense is more the rule. Does a responsible parent want heroin and crack in school? Do they want a safe environment? The answers are obvious to me. But I speak from a more urbanized area where maintaining a controlled orderly class is problem enough without adding guns and drugs to the mix. But then I believe that responsible parenting is also an issue in such areas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T07:19:09-08:00","id":64821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=64810#post64810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hate to break it to you, but guns are lumped into the whole &quot;Zero Tolerance&quot; thing. After all there are two categories regarding it and one of them is guns. The other is drugs.<br /> Things have dropped a bit since such policies have been adopted: <img src=\"http://www.drugabuse.gov/sites/default/files/styles/content_image_landscape/public/pastyearusealldrugs.jpeg?itok=1xh2T850\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Is it because of such policies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I am well familiar with this. Lack of evidence to support something so you haul out a correlation and claim it as a cause. By the same logic the decrease in pirates in the world is causing global warming. <br /> <br /> Please try again when you actually have something.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=64810#post64810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless, Responsible parents want a safe environment for their children. An environment where teachers can maintain order. Difficult in an urban school which is something I'm pretty sure no one in this thread knows much about. But everyone hears plenty about school shootings in rural and suburban areas, where that sort of thing tends to happen the most.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great Rhetoric. When all else fails, throw in references to threatening children, claim great personal experience. I'm half-surprised you didn't throw a flag in the background and start chanting god bless america.<br /> <br /> As I have said multiple times, nobody here is saying the environment should not be safe. Nobody is saying we let kids carry guns in class. The only thing we are against here is Zero Tolerance polices. Which *you* have admitted have caused harm to students (granted not a lot of them) and we are calling on *you* to point to any proof that they do a better job than the teacher/principal based discretion policies that were in place before.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=64810#post64810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it seems to me that is what we have today; discretion. As long as it doesn't endanger funding (Federal law) that is what's going on today.<br /> Yes, there seems to be the relative few that gets the media parade. But out of thousands of schools, typically laughed off as rural backwards localities.<br /> <br /> I should hope that common sense is more the rule. Does a responsible parent want heroin and crack in school? Do they want a safe environment? The answers are obvious to me. But I speak from a more urbanized area where maintaining a controlled orderly class is problem enough without adding guns and drugs to the mix. But then I believe that responsible parenting is also an issue in such areas.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would love it if common sense were the rule, unfortunately you keep arguing for Zero Tolerance policies instead of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T11:57:28-08:00","id":65039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=64810#post64810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't do youtube, especially when someone can't properly argue the point himself. (But I suppose that's an opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The definition I gave of 'Zero Tolerance' is a point of fact. It cannot be hyperbole. It is unarguable.<br /> <br /> Moreover, here is a link for you: <a href=\"http://legalclips.nsba.org/2011/05/11/delaware-school-district-backs-off-zero-tolerance-polices-after-student-lawsuit-and-federal-discrimination-investigation/\" target=\"_blank\">http://legalclips.nsba.org/2011/05/1...investigation/</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Delaware school district backs off zero tolerance polices after student lawsuit and federal discrimination investigation </div> </div> </div>Another link: <a href=\"https://www.aclu.org/racial-justice_drug-law-reform_immigrants-rights_national-security/aclu-files-lawsuit-behalf-maine-h\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.aclu.org/racial-justice_...behalf-maine-h</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Once again, a zero tolerance policy has stripped school administrators of their own ability to use good judgment,&quot; said Richard L. O'Meara, Legal Director of the ACLU of Maine. &quot;Not only did school administrators, in Tracy's case, fail to notify her of campus policy, she was subjected to the misinterpretation of that policy by the very people who are supposed to be enforcing it.&quot; O'Meara said that the school district's expulsion of the student for violation of its local &quot;zero tolerance&quot; policy plainly violates Maine's state law governing school expulsions and the student's due process rights. </div> </div> </div>And a third link: <a href=\"http://www.sj-r.com/x450313345/School-district-sued-over-zero-tolerance-weapons-policy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.sj-r.com/x450313345/Schoo...weapons-policy</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The lawsuit, filed by the boy\u2019s father, Allen Mueller, claims the school district\u2019s policy is unfair because it does not take into account intent or mitigating circumstances, such as a student\u2019s academic, extracurricular or disciplinary record. </div> </div> </div>Maybe a fourth link: <a href=\"http://www.abajournal.com/news/article/some_schools_abandon_zero_tolerance_policies_partly_because_of_lawsuits/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.abajournal.com/news/artic...e_of_lawsuits/</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some schools are abandoning zero-tolerance policies in favor of a more nuanced approach to discipline, and lawsuits are partly the reason. </div> </div> </div>A fifth link: <a href=\"http://thinkprogress.org/justice/2014/01/08/3133631/doj-schools-stop-sending-kids-jail-breaking-rules/\" target=\"_blank\">http://thinkprogress.org/justice/201...reaking-rules/</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Kids are arrested for wearing the wrong color socks and starting food fights. In Meridian, Miss., it was school officials \u2013 not police \u2013 who determined who should be arrested. Schools seeking to discipline students called the police, and police policy was to <a href=\"http://thinkprogress.org/justice/2012/11/27/1239111/mississippi-county-jails-kids-for-school-dress-code-violations-tardiness-doj-alleges/\" target=\"_blank\">arrest all children referred to the agency</a>, according to a Department of Justice lawsuit that was <a href=\"http://thinkprogress.org/justice/2013/03/25/1764821/mississippi-school-district-agrees-stop-suspending-kids-for-dress-code-violations/\" target=\"_blank\">settled last March</a>. The lawsuit called the the city\u2019s police department a de facto \u201ctaxi service\u201d shuttling students from school to juvenile detention centers. In Texas, another DOJ lawsuit highlighted one county\u2019s policy of filing <a href=\"http://thinkprogress.org/justice/2013/06/14/2156481/texas-county-uses-electronic-system-to-file-automatic-criminal-charges-for-student-truancy-complaint-alleges/\" target=\"_blank\">automatic criminal charges against students</a> for truancy. And in Florida, Broward County agreed in November to reform its policy after a spate of arrests for rule violations as minor as <a href=\"http://thinkprogress.org/justice/2013/11/05/2889831/florida-school-prison-pipeline-reform/\" target=\"_blank\">starting a food fight</a>. </div> </div> </div>A sixth for good measure: <a href=\"http://www.npr.org/templates/story/story.php?storyId=250395166\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.npr.org/templates/story/s...ryId=250395166</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The police chief of Miami Gardens, Florida has stepped down over allegations that his officers have been violating civil rights. The town is just north of Miami and it's been struggling with a string of deadly shootings. In response, it began what it calls zero tolerance operations, including arrests even for misdemeanors. Which in turn has led to a federal lawsuit. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1592,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","user":"Jack","date":". 02-04-2014, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T15:27:42-08:00","id":65190,"title":"","content":"*reads his thread and weeps*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/219-zid","name":"Zid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T16:15:37-08:00","id":65210,"title":"","content":"*shrugs* The laws won't change anytime soon. A handful of stories won't change things. They never do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T00:17:43-08:00","id":65458,"title":"","content":"No.<br /> <br /> The War on Drugs set the stage for zero tolerance policies in Colorado. Evidently, Colorado have recently changed their laws regarding recreational cannabis and done away with Zero Tolerance, legalising recreational cannabis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Reagan\u2019s demand side initiatives focused on \u201cgetting tough\u201d on drugs. The program became known as the \u201czero tolerance\u201d program, where punitive measures against users were emphasized. </div> </div> </div>reference: <a href=\"http://www.stanford.edu/class/e297c/poverty_prejudice/paradox/htele.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.stanford.edu/class/e297c/...dox/htele.html</a><br /> <br /> reference: <a href=\"http://www.drugpolicy.org/new-solutions-drug-policy/brief-history-drug-war\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.drugpolicy.org/new-soluti...story-drug-war</a><br /> <br /> reference: <a href=\"http://1.bp.blogspot.com/-bP6k59dMHBI/UnQmzKaljjI/AAAAAAAAZUA/3ZDsMcXw4d0/s400/grumpy-cat-8141_preview_zps9177ab07.png\" target=\"_blank\">http://1.bp.blogspot.com/-bP6k59dMHB...ps9177ab07.png</a><br /> <br /> reference: <a href=\"http://www.libertyforall.net/colorados-war-on-drugs-a-fiscal-nightmare/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.libertyforall.net/colorad...cal-nightmare/</a><br /> <br /> Furthermore, here are a couple more damning quotes:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tough school discipline codes like zero-tolerance policies and mandatory suspensions for even minor infractions may have significant costs and glaring inequities. </div> </div> </div>link: <a href=\"http://www.csmonitor.com/USA/Education/2014/0108/School-discipline-New-US-guidelines-shift-away-from-zero-tolerance-policies-video\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.csmonitor.com/USA/Educati...policies-video</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> School districts with \u201czero tolerance\u201d policies are not using common sense and good judgment, said David Riley, chief probation officer of the Bexar County Juvenile Probation Department. While the concept is noble, he said, students are often hurt by its misapplication.<br /> <br /> Riley told the committee that a school district had referred a 14-year old asthmatic middle school student \u2013 who had never been in trouble before \u2013 to the Bexar County JJAEP because she allowed her best friend, also an asthmatic, to use her inhaler. The girl was suspended for one year and charged with a felony for distributing a controlled substance.<br /> <br /> After unsuccessfully appealing to the school district, the parents persuaded the school board to reinstate their child in school and clear her record. The student spent 3 months in JJAEP, which is meant for the most violent juvenile offenders. </div> </div> </div>link: <a href=\"http://www.texaszerotolerance.com/News/Newsarticles/Testimony_SEC.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.texaszerotolerance.com/Ne...imony_SEC.html</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1592,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","user":"Jack","date":". 02-05-2014, 06:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T22:48:28-08:00","id":73561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5001-teenager-scares-the-living-out-of-me?p=63034#post63034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most parents know beforehand that they have to communicate any medical problems with the school before their child attend to begin with. Any parent that stupid not to know...makes me reconsider the validity of eugenics.<br /> And if there's a school without any form of nurse/doctor in it, is a school that isn't legitimate in any state.<br /> <br /> Lot of hyperbole being thrown in this thread. How can anyone take that seriously?<br /> <br /> I had some damn good teachers in high school.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I've read the &quot;Zero Tolerance&quot; comments...and I know this has been closed, but I'm going to comment on the nurse/doctors in school thing above.<br /> <br /> The local school where I live has butchered their budget to the extent that they only have a nurse twice a week, which is pretty useless. Their policy is that ALL student medicine must be stored in the nurses office and can only be given by the Nurse or a Parent. Well...when the Nurse is not there 3-days out of the week, a Parent <b>must</b> come to the school and give the medication, no matter what. If they are unable to come, then EMS is called...but not until after a parent is called, which wastes valuable time.<br /> <br /> We pulled our Daughter out of school last year <i>(partially because of this)</i> because she has severe Asthma that can come on rapidly, and when it does it can crush her heart <i>(She has a very tiny hole in her heart that the Dr's don't want to operate on yet for various health reasons)</i>. We can't make it to the School in time to administer the medication, and the School won't let her self-medicate, which she has learned to do even at 9-years of age <i>(Zero Tolerance at work here)</i>.<br /> <br /> Other reasons to pull her out? Oh, the not-so-normal 1st Grade stuff: Bullying in 1st -- bruises on her back, bloody smears on her face, name calling, boys telling her to &quot;suck my #w8#&quot; <i>(Yeah...in 1st Grade)</i>. The teachers didn't do anything when it was reported by her and us <i>(&quot;They come from nice families. They wouldn't do anything like that.&quot;)</i>. When she defended herself from being attacked <i>(again, after telling the teachers)</i>, <b>she</b> was the one who got in trouble <i>(Zero Tolerance Policy again)</i>. Let's just say that a &quot;One-On-One&quot; conversation between myself and the Principle solved the issue...everything stopped cold turkey. But it shouldn't ever have happened in the first place, and if it did it should have stopped immediately when it was reported.<br /> <br /> Anyway...Not every Parent in this sort of situation is &quot;Stupid&quot; as there are often extenuating circumstances like &quot;Zero Tolerance&quot; policies that tie their hands.<br /> <br /> Eugenik aus dem neunzehnten Jahrhundert, ist dies eine neue \u00c4ra. Werden wir f\u00fcr Unebenheiten auf V\u00f6lker K\u00f6pfe neben sich? Bitte, nicht \u00fcber einen Kamm scheren uns um in die Vernichtungslager noch recht geschickt werden, ja? Wir sind nicht die Menschen in Amerika f\u00fcr Dummheit t\u00f6ten, mein Freund zu verstehen?<br /> <br /> Frieden.<br /> <br /> Peace.<br /> <br /> <br /> ~ N<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S.: Forgive my German. It is most definitely not my first language, and it is pretty bad. I apologize if its spelling, syntax &amp; language structure offends. I try my best...but at least it is better than my Chinese <i>(Which my Wife is doing her best to teach me. My Children are light years ahead of me...)</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}